    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Coordinator--Student-Operations_JR104398": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Student Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information Organization's Summary Statement: Education Abroad (EA) is the University of Maryland’s hub for global learning overseas, connecting students with credit-bearing, culturally immersive study abroad programs that complement the curricula of our academic programs. Rooted in our commitment to access and belonging, we design diverse, high-quality programs that develop our students’ intercultural and solution-focused skills that shape their journey to become effective citizens, professionals, and human beings. As part of Maryland Global, EA is a vibrant community of professionals who foster a collaborative and innovative workplace where staff and faculty thrive while shaping the future of global education. Position  Summary The Student Operations Coordinator oversees enrollment management processes, program administration, student services, outreachactivities, and departmental initiatives that advance student participation in global learning opportunities. Reporting to the Assistant Director for Operations, the Coordinator works collaboratively with advising, operations, and program management staﬀ to ensure eﬃcient delivery of Education Abroad services and a positive student experience. Essential   Duties/Responsibilities Study Abroad Course Information Management  (35%) Manage the workﬂow for study abroad transfer-credit course evaluations, exercising independent judgment to establishpriorities, identify workﬂow deﬁciencies, resolve process issues, and ensure accurate and timely coordination between Education Abroad and Transfer Credit Services. Monitor and analyze large datasets in the study abroad course database to proactively identify expiring course approval records, emerging academic trends, gaps in course oﬀerings, and other issues aﬀecting program administration; provide recommendations to Global Learning Advisors regarding curriculum development and strategic program needs. Audit student course registrations against approved course-evaluation information, identify discrepancies or potential academic-record issues, determine appropriate corrective actions, and coordinate resolution with relevant oﬃces. Records & Registration  (25%) Administer and oversee student registration and records processes for Education Abroad programs, identifying registration issues and determining appropriate  resolutions. Interpret and implement established Education Abroad operating practices related to registration, records, insurance, and program readiness, recommending modiﬁcations to procedures when existing practices do not adequately address operational needs. Conduct comprehensive audits of student academic records, assess the accuracy and completeness of credit and gradeinformation, identify operational deﬁciencies, and initiate corrective actions or recommendations to ensure the integrity of  records. Other duties as  assigned. Advising & Outreach  (25%) Develop student-facing resources and recommend outreach opportunities, including presentations, webinars, videos,guides, and other materials in support of Education Abroad's strategic objectives. Participate in strategic planning initiatives focused on study abroad experience, identifying opportunities forimprovement and developing recommendations to improve communications. Serve as a co-lead for large scale Education Abroad sponsored events including Study Abroad Fairs and visa services events, coordinating operations involving internal and external stakeholders. Other duties as  assigned. Student-facing Operations  (15%) Serve as an administrative resource for complex student and stakeholder inquiries, independently assessing the nature ofissues, determining appropriate responses or courses of action, and resolving matters within the scope of delegated authority. Evaluate proposed system and workﬂow changes and provide recommendations regarding content improvements that enhance the student experience. Other duties as  assigned. Additional Information : UMD will not sponsor the successful candidate for work authorization in the United States now or in the future. Required Application Materials : Resume Cover Letter 3 Professional References Best Consideration Date :  September 29, 2026 Posting Close Date :  September 29, 2026 Open Until Filled :  No Physical Demands :  Work is performed in an office environment and requires the ability to operate standard office equipment and keyboards. Must have the ability to walk short distances, and/or drive a vehicle to deliver and pick up materials. Preferred  Qualiﬁcations: One year of experience in higher education administration, student services, international education, program coordination, enrollment management, or advising. Study, volunteer or work experience in an international or intercultural setting Demonstrated commitment to expanding access to educational and global learning opportunities Demonstrated experience working with a student information system Demonstrated experience managing and analysing large datasets. Experience with the Google suite, with strong skills in Google Sheets. Ability to problem solve and implement solutions with strong attention to detail. Licenses/ Certifications : N/A Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: One (1) year of professional administrative or coordinator experience. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES:   Knowledge of best practices in organization, administration, and customer service. Knowledge of proper protocol in dealing with confidential information. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office and Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Slides, Forms, etc.) Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Ability to multitask while demonstrating a commitment to customer service. Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Department SVPAAP-OIA-Education Abroad Worker Sub-Type Staff Contractual (C2) (Fixed Term) Salary Range $55,000-$60,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Staff Contractual CII benefits, select this link   . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Electronics-Technician-III_JR104879": {
      "title": "Electronics Technician III",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: Under the general supervision of the Facilities Performance Group Operations Manager, the Electronics Technician III is assigned on a daily basis to maintain and repair utility meters, HVAC, lighting, electrical, building automation, and devices that acquire data from these systems. The Electronics Technician III will review and ensure operational readiness of new and existing electro-mechanical systems and complete checkout of these systems as needed. The Electronics Technician III will also develop skills to use computers and mobile devices to program, operate, test, and calibrate the electrical and HVAC metering devices used by the Facilities Performance Group to measure campus energy usage and system performance. Physical Demands: Physical demands associated with this position include extensive walking, lifting & carrying heavy-weighted materials (up to 50 lbs.), as well as bending over to record field data. Must be able to bend, stoop, use power tools, drive motor vehicles, and climb ladders and scaffolding to work at heights up to 20 feet. Ability to work in, on around, over and under fixed equipment and machinery; to manipulate heavy equipment, tools, and supplies and/or exert force up to 50 lbs.; to concurrently manipulate multiple controls on equipment and machinery; to work in hazardous or irritating environments, confined spaces, adverse weather or temperature conditions; to wear and work in personal protective equipment. Incumbent is deemed an Essential: Weather/Other employee subject to a 24-hour day, 7-day week span of operation. This position is telework eligible. Preferences: • Bachelor’s or associate degree or vocational school or technical education that relates to this position is highly desired. • Certification or license in HVAC, Electrical, or Building Automation Systems. • Training in one or more of the following areas: utility metering, electronics, steam boilers, HVAC, electrical or building automation. • Ability to integrate devices (meters preferred) with Building Automation Systems residing on a large campus Ethernet LAN and communicating using Modbus RTU and/or BACNet MSTP protocols. • Ability to install rigid or EMT conduit. • Previous experience with installing equipment and meters. • Ability to adapt to changing environments. • Knowledge of HVAC pneumatic controls. • Knowledge of safe work practices for one or more of the following utilities: electrical, steam, natural gas, water, and heating and cooling water. • Training in electrical/electronics, installation methods, schematics, and wiring (preferably metering); be a qualified person with technical education to work with systems at voltages greater than 50 (Safety); have training and a detailed understanding of at least one of the utilities that is metered (electric, steam, thermal energy, water). • Ability to use hand tools, electrical testing equipment, and calibration equipment such as VOM meters, AMP probes, oscilloscopes, and Field Programming Interfaces. • Ability to document meter setup parameters, maintain work history, and calibration database for meters in AssetWorks AIM (automated work management system). • Ability to monitor and check out HVAC systems, lighting, building, and lighting controls. • Ability to follow sequences for electro-mechanical systems to confirm proper operation as intended. • Skill in the use of computers for Building Automation System (BAS), Microsoft Word, Box, Excel, and email, and to set up or program meters and/or demonstrate programming of similar devices. Licenses/ Certifications: The incumbent must possess a valid driver's license, as duties require travel to and from meetings and project sites, both on and off campus. If driving a state vehicle, the incumbent must possess a valid Maryland Class C driver's license (or equivalent) with fewer than six (6) points. Minimum Qualifications EDUCATION: High School Diploma or GED. EXPERIENCE: Six years in related work. OTHER: REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE/SKILLS/ABILITIES: Thorough knowledge of the basic electronics principles and the materials, elements, and products applicable to the area of specialization. Thorough knowledge and skill in the application of principles of applied arithmetic, geometry, and trigonometry and the system of measure applicable to the specialization; in reading and interpreting technical specifications and drawings; in fabricating and assembling electromechanical and structural components and equipment from drawings and specifications; in setting up and calibrating instruments and preparing equipment for testing; in operating equipment applicable to the job according to standard safety practices. Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing; to prepare reports and detailed procedures; to use personal computers; to lead and train others in technical electronics support work; to work in, on, around, over and under fixed equipment and machinery; to manipulate heavy equipment, tools, and supplies and/or exert force up to 50 lbs.; to concurrently manipulate multiple controls on equipment and machinery; to work in hazardous or irritating environments; confined spaces; and adverse weather or temperature conditions; to wear and work in personal protective equipment. OTHER: Except for qualifications established by law, additional related experience and formal education in which one has gained the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for full performance of the work of the job class may be substituted for the education or experience requirement on a year-for-year basis with 30 college credits being equivalent to one year of experience. CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT: Candidates selected for employment may be subject to medical inquiries and/or medical examinations to determine ability to perform the job. A non-commercial Class C or equivalent driver's license valid in the State of Maryland may be required. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: N/A   Best Consideration Date: N/A   Posting Close Date: 9/18/2026   Open Until Filled: N/A Visa Requirement: This position does not provide visa sponsorship.    Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department VPA-FM-E&E-Facility Performance Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $60,673.00 - $72,808.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Nonexempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/UHR-Labor-Relations-Consultant_JR104438-1": {
      "title": "UHR Labor Relations Consultant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary University Human Resources (UHR) has an exciting opportunity for a HR professional to serve as a Labor Relations Consultant within the UHR Labor Relations team. The Labor Relations Consultant is responsible for providing professional support to the Program Director, Labor Relations. The incumbent in this role will have the opportunity to foster positive working relationships with labor unions, resolve union disputes and ensure compliance with labor laws, regulations and collective bargaining agreements. The ideal candidate will have experience providing professional support in a high pace, high volume environment while maintaining strong communication with unions and leadership and confidentiality of sensitive information. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Five (5) years of professional human resources experience in the areas of employee or labor relations. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of human resources policies and procedures, and federal, state, and other applicable human resources related laws, rules, regulations, and ordinances. Knowledge of employment laws and regulations, including those pertaining to collective bargaining and employer-employee relations. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office and Google Workspace products. Skill in oral and written communication. Ability to analyze and solve problems. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Additional Job Details Preferences: NA Required Application Materials: Resume , Cover Letter , List of References Best Consideration Date: September 17th, 2026 Posting Close Date: NA Open Until Filled: Yes Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial 