    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Research-Software-and-Data-Engineer_JR104853": {
      "title": "Research Software and Data Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary This position is available within the University of Maryland’s Division of Information Technology (DIT). Overview: The Research Computing team, part of the University of Maryland’s Division of Information Technology (DIT), designs and supports advanced technology systems and services used by researchers at UMD - a top 20 public research institution. The Research Software and Data Engineer will play a key role in designing, implementing, and supporting research cyberinfrastructure, software, and data-facing solutions. Primary Responsibilities: The Research Software and Data Engineer's primary responsibilities will be to work with researchers to design, plan, and implement secure, compliant, and well-engineered software, data workflows, and data science-focused solutions that enrich research productivity, reliability, and reproducibility. The engineer will be part of short- to long-term projects. The work will also include consulting with researchers across disciplines in order to deeply understand their software and data needs and to identify and explain solutions. Additional Responsibilities: The Research Software and Data Engineer will work with other team members to offer a wide range of related training workshops and to help bring a mature project management approach to research software work on campus, contributing toward software design and project planning and tracking. The Engineer will also write code to automate cloud account management, such as provisioning new cloud accounts. The Engineer will work with researchers to adapt existing workflows to cloud environments. As a Research Computing team member, they will provide technical expertise and insight to teams and projects alongside research programs, collaborate across multiple units in the Division of IT and the University, and help researchers navigate the tools, processes, and services available to them. **This position is considered essential and may be required to work at the normal work location or an alternative location during a major catastrophic event, weather emergency, or other operational emergency to help maintain the continuity of University services.** **May be required to work evenings, nights, weekends, or different shifts for extended periods.** Physical Demands: Predominantly operates in an office environment. Some periods of time may be spent in computer room and communications equipment spaces for installation, testing, and troubleshooting. Some work (less than 5%) requires moving and lifting of heavy computing equipment. Licenses/Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Three to five years experience working in software and data engineering environments. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. Knowledge of research computing technologies: o Batch processing o Relational Database architectures o Data Science tools o Data pipelines, ETL, and data workflows Knowledge of machine learning frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, and JAX. Knowledge of creating and operating container based infrastructure; knowledge of Docker or similar technology. Knowledge of GPU programming. Skill in programming, particularly in the languages used in our computational research applications (Julia programming language, C/C++, FORTRAN, python, R). Skilled at providing technical solutions to complex problems in diverse computing environments. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Google and Microsoft Office products. Ability to learn new programming languages and technologies beyond area of core knowledge. Ability to effectively communicate technical concepts with non-technical audiences. Ability to multitask while demonstrating a commitment to customer service. Additional Job Details Preferences: Thorough knowledge of software lifecycle and software engineering best practices (sprints, code reviews, testing) Thorough knowledge of data science methods Ability to communicate with both technical and non-technical clients Experience with version control systems and issue trackers Experience with cloud platforms, to include code development, familiarity with APIs, user management Experience implementing/operating with controls for NIST SP 800-171, HIPAA Security and Privacy rules, or similar levels of security and compliance Required Application Materials:  Cover Letter Resume List of Three References Additional Information: Please note that all positions within the Division of Information Technology (DIT) have an in person component with expected time in our College Park, MD location per week. Telework is not a guaranteed work arrangement. Visa Sponsorship Information: DIT will not sponsor the successful candidate for work authorization in the United States now or in the future. F1 STEM OPT support is not available for this position. Best Consideration Date:  9/23/26 Posting Close Date:  N/A Open Until Filled:  Yes Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department DIT-EE-Research Computing Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $105,800 - $126,960 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Associate-Director--State-Government-Relations_JR104856": {
      "title": "Associate Director, State Government Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Associate Director for State Government Relations works under the direction of the Director of State and Local Government Relations to advocate for the University of Maryland’s priorities with the Maryland General Assembly, the Governor’s Office, state agencies, and other state governmental stakeholders. This position serves as a primary day-to-day liaison between the University and state legislators, legislative staff, executive branch officials, and agency staff. The Associate Director supports the full range of state government relations activities, including legislative monitoring and analysis, advocacy strategy, testimony and policy material development, relationship-building, budget and regulatory tracking, and coordination of state government requests involving University leadership, faculty, staff, students, and administrative units. The Associate Director plays a central role in the University’s annual legislative session strategy and maintains year-round engagement with state government to advance University priorities, identify opportunities for collaboration, anticipate risks, and shape policy outcomes. As appropriate, this position may represent the University before the General Assembly, state agencies, external coalitions, and stakeholder groups. This role works closely with other members of the Office of Government Relations, including colleagues responsible for strategic initiatives, community engagement, federal relations, local government relations, and government communications, to ensure coordinated and consistent engagement across all levels of government. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Five (5) years of professional experience in legislative affairs working directly with lawmakers on policy or budget matters. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of state and local government structures, legislative processes, public policy development, and governmental relations practices. Knowledge of legislative affairs strategies, advocacy principles, and approaches for engaging with elected officials, government agencies, and other governmental stakeholders. Knowledge of higher education issues, institutional priorities, and policies impacting public universities. Skill in monitoring, analyzing, and summarizing legislative proposals, regulations, and public policy issues affecting organizational priorities. Skill in developing written communications, legislative briefings, reports, presentations, and other materials for internal and external audiences. Skill in establishing and maintaining effective working relationships with elected officials, legislative staff, government agencies, and community stakeholders. Ability to interpret complex legislative and policy information and evaluate potential impacts on institutional programs and priorities. Ability to coordinate government relations activities, including legislative tracking, stakeholder engagement, and advocacy efforts. Ability to communicate effectively and professionally while representing institutional interests with diverse audiences. Additional Job Details Preferences: Bachelor’s degree in political science, public policy, public administration, communications, law, higher education administration, or a related field Direct experience working in the Maryland General Assembly, the Governor’s Office, a Maryland state agency, a legislative committee office, a public university system, or a government relations office. Existing relationships with members, staff, or leadership of the Maryland General Assembly, the Governor’s Office, Maryland executive branch agencies, or statewide policy organizations. Experience in higher education, a research institution, public university, nonprofit, association, or public-sector government relations environment. Familiarity with state higher education policy, including operating budget, capital budget, University System of Maryland governance, research funding, financial aid, workforce development, and public university issues. Experience drafting testimony, preparing witnesses, supporting amendment negotiations, and developing legislative advocacy strategies. Experience coordinating legislative visits, advocacy days, campus briefings, stakeholder convenings, or grassroots/alumni advocacy programs. Familiarity with legislative tracking systems, policy databases, lobbying compliance practices, or government relations CRM tools. Required Application Materials: Resume, Cover Letter, and List of three (3) Professional References Best Consideration Date: September 27, 2026 Posting Close Date: N/A Open Until Filled: Yes Physical Demands: Predominantly works in an office environment. Will require the ability to regularly travel throughout the State of Maryland. Ability to walk and stand for extended periods of time, both indoors and outdoors. This position will require occasional evening work hours. Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required Yes For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department Pres-President's Office Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $106,800 - $128,160 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Mid-Senior-Technical-Program-Manager--TPM---Sr-Faculty-Specialist_JR104811": {
      "title": "Mid/Senior Technical Program Manager (TPM)/ Sr. Faculty Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The A. James Clark School of Engineering at the University of Maryland serves as the catalyst for high-quality research, innovation, and learning, delivering on a promise that all graduates will leave ready to impact the Grand Challenges (e.g., energy, environment, security, and human health) of the 21st century. The Clark School is dedicated to leading and transforming the engineering discipline and profession, to accelerating entrepreneurship, and to transforming research and learning activities into new innovations that benefit millions. The Center for Advanced Transportation Technology (CATT) Laboratory is the industry leader for transportation information analysis, visualization, and user interface design. We provide cutting-edge analytics products and an integrated suite of situational awareness tools for transportation practitioners. These products and services are rapidly changing the way governments operate and make decisions. You can learn more about our products at https://ritis.org/. We receive hundreds of gigabytes of transportation data daily, making our petabytes of archived data likely the largest collection of traffic data in the world. Our clients use our software to monitor real-time operations and analyze historical data to generate valuable insights. Our work saves taxpayers money, improves the environment, and saves lives! We’re as passionate about transportation as we are about building great software. We care about building usable, stable, and secure software to analyze massive amounts of data. We use cutting-edge tech to build and maintain our software. We have a mature development process and use industry best practices to build the best software possible. Our team is composed of application developers, analysts, UX designers, data scientists, IT, quality assurance specialists, and customer support operating in an Agile environment. Our office is in College Park near the University of Maryland, easily accessible by DC Metro, MARC train, bus, car, and bike. Local employees are welcome to work in our office, or other locations, with a flexible schedule around our core hours. We also have many employees who are fully remote and work from different states. UMD requires all employees to live in the US, and we periodically bring remote employees to work with colleagues on-site. We believe varied perspectives build better products, are proud to have a diverse team, and encourage people of all backgrounds to apply. When you join our team, you will work to define, document, and test a wide variety of transportation data analytics and operations applications. You will learn new skills and stay current with industry best practices and emerging technologies. Position Summary The Center for Advanced Transportation Technology Laboratory (CATT Lab) is seeking an experienced Mid/Senior Technical Program Manager (TPM) to lead the planning, execution, and delivery of complex software and analytical solutions. The TPM serves as the primary liaison between technical teams, product stakeholders, leadership, and customers to ensure successful delivery of CATT Lab products. This role is responsible for program planning, project execution, stakeholder engagement, and resource coordination across multiple projects and technical disciplines. Approximately 80% of the role focuses on project and program management, with up to 20% dedicated to product ownership responsibilities. The ideal candidate has experience managing multidisciplinary technical teams, quickly learning new programs and technologies, and working effectively in environments with evolving priorities and competing demands. The TPM will oversee one or more of the following technical teams: Software Engineering Data Science and Analytics Data Architecture and Platform UX/UI IT Operations and Infrastructure Customer Support Physical Demands: Sedentary work performed in an office environment. Regularly required to communicate and exchange information and to use technology/devices. Position can be 100% remote (US based only) Minimum Qualifications Master's degree. Five (5) or more years of experience in program management, project management, or product management roles. Experience managing multiple concurrent technical projects or programs with competing priorities. Experience managing complex technical projects involving software development, analytics, data platforms, infrastructure, or operational systems. Experience leading multidisciplinary technical teams with five (5) or more technical resources. Experience communicating technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, including executive leadership and customers. Experience with Agile, Scrum, Kanban, or hybrid methodologies. Experience using Jira, Confluence, or comparable tools. Strong communication, facilitation, and stakeholder management skills. Preferences: Bachelor’s or Master's degree in Project Management, Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, Analytics, or a related discipline. Eight (8) or more years of experience in program management, project management, or product management roles. Experience serving in both project management and product ownership capacities. Experience managing technical teams delivering software, analytics, or decision-support solutions. Experience with on-premise and/or hybrid infrastructure environments. Demonstrated ability to quickly learn new technologies, business domains, and customer programs. Familiarity with GovRAMP, FedRAMP, NIST 800-53, FISMA, or related security and compliance frameworks. PMP, PMI-ACP, CSM, or comparable certification. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: CV/Resume Cover Letter (optional) References upon request. Professional Statement-required upon completion of the interview process and before an offer 2 External Letters-required upon completion of the interview process and before an offer Best Consideration date:  9/8/26  Posting close date: Open until filled     Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ENGR-Civil-Center for Advanced Transportation Technology Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $120,000-$175,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Agent-Associate--Agriculture-and-Food-Systems_JR104840": {
      "title": "Agent Associate, Agriculture and Food Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: University of Maryland Extension (UME) is a statewide, non-formal education system within the College of Agriculture and Natural Resources and the University of Maryland Eastern Shore. UME educational programs and problem-solving assistance are available to citizens and are based on the research and experience of land grant universities such as the University of Maryland, College Park. In Maryland, UME employs approximately 200 faculty and approximately 200 support staff and contractual employees located at the University of Maryland, College Park; University of Maryland Eastern Shore; 23 counties; Baltimore City; and four research and education centers. Many UME faculty members located on the College Park and Eastern Shore campuses have joint appointments with research and academic programs. These joint appointments promote the exchange of knowledge between the universities and among academic specialties. Position Summary/Purpose of Position: This position is located in the University of Maryland Extension Office in Prince George’s County, Maryland. The position will support the Prince George’s County Agriculture and Food Systems Extension Program. The Educator will provide coordination and programmatic support for agronomy and horticultural crops, livestock, small farm and alternative agriculture, marketing, urban agriculture, and farm and agribusiness development in Prince George’s County, and in collaboration with Extension faculty in the Capitol Cluster. Responsibilities: ● Work with University of Maryland Extension (UME) Agriculture and Food Systems action teams to develop, promote, implement, and evaluate educational programs for agronomic and horticultural crop production, livestock production, small-scale farming and alternative agriculture enterprises, urban agriculture, and farm and agribusiness management to provide educational opportunities for clientele related to agricultural production, business management, and marketing in Prince George’s County, the Capitol Cluster, and across the state. ● Deliver programs in crop production, farm and agribusiness management, integrated pest management, pesticide safety, livestock production, nutrient management, and natural resource conservation for agricultural producers in Prince George’s County, the Capitol Cluster, and across the state. ● Provide training and recertification opportunities for certified private pesticide applicators and nutrient management voucher holders. ● Develop Extension programs that improve the financial viability of farms through business and cooperative development, grain marketing clubs, sustainable agriculture initiatives, community organization, and continuing education for producers. ● Work collaboratively with Maryland-National Capital Park and Planning Commission Prince George's County Planning Department and Southern and Central Maryland Agricultural Marketing Professionals (AMPs) to develop, implement, and evaluate economic development initiatives including, but not limited to, agri-tourism, wholesale markets, direct marketing, and value-added agriculture projects. ● Prepare information for the media, which may include news articles, press releases, and newsletters. ● Remain current in assigned subject matter areas and participate in relevant professional improvement opportunities. ● Develop and implement Extension program marketing and public relations activities. ● Develop grant-funded projects to enhance and expand applied research and educational programs. ● Develop strong relationships with local agriculture organizations, including attendance and participation at Maryland-National Capital Park and Planning Commission Prince George's County Planning Department, Farm Bureau, and Soil Conservation District meetings, as required. ● Develop creative and scholarly activities that are validated by peers and communicated, such as educational materials published and adopted by others, Extension and research publications, conference posters, and professional presentations and participation in applied research. ● Serve as a consultant to county government on the issues of land use, planning, and agriculture and food systems. ● Serve on city, county, and regional agricultural committees. Physical Demands: ● This position frequently presents information through vocal and written communication to individuals of various ages, socio-economic, and educational backgrounds. ● A routine part of this position's responsibilities would be to transport materials to and from field research plots and teaching/event locations, including loading and unloading the vehicle. The employee will frequently lift and/or move items weighing up to 20 pounds. Set up and teardown of research machinery, project displays, and tables and chairs will be necessary at many teaching sites. ● This position requires the employee to work outdoors conducting field research, delivering programs, and teaching at events. This may occur during very hot and/or inclement weather. ● Visual acuity is required for preparing and analyzing written or computer data and presentations. ● Able to traverse farm fields and uneven terrain. Qualifications: Required– ● BS degree in agricultural education, agronomy, animal science, horticulture, agricultural business, or related field and some experience in agricultural rural development or agribusiness. ● Three years of leadership and management experience that demonstrates the ability to work well with farmers and community leaders. ● Knowledge and use of computer technology for educational programming and management. ● Plant diagnostic skills, such as identifying weeds, insects, and diseases. ● Personal transportation and valid driver’s license required. Must be willing to travel throughout the Cluster, as well as the state of Maryland as needed. ● Flexible work schedule required for delivering evening and weekend educational programs and activities as determined by clientele availability and needs. ● Must become a certified Maryland nutrient management advisor/consultant and obtain a commercial pesticide applicators license in category-10 public agency. ● This position is subject to a Criminal History Record Check. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and clearance of the Criminal History Record Check. Preferences: ● M.S. degree in agricultural education, agronomy, animal science, horticulture, agricultural business, or related field. ● Extension or similar work experience in formal or non-formal community-based education. ● Demonstrated ability to acquire grant funding. ● Ability and experience in using social media to engage clientele. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Additional Job Details Location: This position is located off-campus at the Prince George's County Extension Office in Clinton, MD. Additional Information: Candidate must be eligible to work in the United States at the time of hiring. The department will not provide sponsorship for work-visa requirements. Required Application Materials: All candidates must apply online. A complete application packet must include the following documents: Cover Letter that addresses the applicant's research and Extension experience and philosophies Resume or Curriculum Vitae (CV) Copies of Transcripts Three (3) examples of Extension materials or outputs Three (3) references , each with name, mailing address, telephone number, and email address. Please note that you may upload multiple documents within the same upload field when submitting your application.   Best Consideration Date: 09/30/2026   Posting Close Date: n/a   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-UME-Prince George's Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range Bachelors range: $49,809 - $63,809, Masters range: $52,059 - $66,059 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Program-Administrative-Specialist_JR104687": {
      "title": "Program Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information Organizational Summary Statement: The Program Administrative Specialist for the Maryland Business Opportunity Center (MBOC) provides specialized administrative, operational, analytical, and client-assessment support to advance MBOC's statewide business assistance mission. Working under limited supervision, the position interprets program guidelines, evaluates client information and documentation, exercises independent judgment in prioritizing work and determining next steps, and supports the Program Director, advisors, partners, and businesses served through MBOC. The role helps ensure efficient program operations, consistent application of requirements, accurate reporting, and effective client service. Essential Duties & Responsibilities 80% Coordinate daily MBOC operations, including schedules, meetings, intake processing, documentation tracking, workflow sequencing, and follow-up activities. Apply established MBOC, SBDC, UMD, and grant-funding requirements; suggest, recommend, and assist in implementing revised procedures and practices that improve efficiency, consistency, and compliance. Maintain accurate client, program, eligibility, metrics, and compliance records in CRM systems, shared drives, and applicable reporting platforms. Conduct initial and ongoing assessments to identify client needs, readiness, barriers, documentation gaps, and appropriate program pathways. Provide substantive guidance regarding procurement readiness, required documentation, registration steps, program expectations, and available resources within established program parameters. Evaluate client submissions and supporting records for completeness, consistency, and alignment with program standards; determine when additional verification or follow-up is needed. Recommend appropriate next steps, solutions, referrals, and technical assistance resources based on client circumstances and program requirements. Determine client submissions are sufficiently complete to advance to advisor review or require additional information before proceeding. Prioritize cases and follow-up actions based on urgency, risk, program impact, deadlines, and operational needs. Interpret and apply program requirements to unique client situations and determine when issues should be escalated to an advisor or program leadership. Use data, research, documentation review, and client interactions to recommend improvements that strengthen efficiency, compliance, documentation quality, and client outcomes. 20% Serve as a liaison among clients, advisors, program staff, statewide partners, community organizations, business-support agencies, and internal departments to facilitate timely communication and coordination. Draft and distribute program announcements, reminders, client updates, and other information resources for staff, partners, and stakeholders. Coordinate logistics for workshops, webinars, outreach events, training sessions, and community engagement activities, including scheduling, materials, and participant communication. Compile and prepare monthly, quarterly, and annual reports using CRM data, staff submissions, and other program information; prepare draft reports, recommendations, and support materials for management. Collect, compile, and organize data for ongoing program activities, studies, plans, budgets, grant proposals, and project proposals; identify trends, gaps, and program needs. Maintain documentation and administrative processes in accordance with applicable federal, state, UMD, SBDC, and grant-funding guidelines and handle sensitive information with tact and discretion. Preferences: Bachelor's degree in business administration, public administration, economics, or related field. Experience supporting small business programs, procurement assistance, economic-development initiatives, or similar business-support services. Experience with CRM or database systems, such as NeoSerra) and familiarity with UMD systems such as Workday, procurement tools, and shared drives. Strong organizational, communication, and problem-solving skills. Knowledge of SBDC, MBOC, APEX, VBOC, or similar small‑business support programs. ​ Physical Demands: The position requires prolonged periods of computer-based work, including typing, data entry, virtual counseling, and report preparation. Telework is a part of the role, but the Program Administrative Specialist must also report to the office periodically for in‐person meetings or administrative needs. A valid driver’s license is required, as the role involves frequent travel within the local community and surrounding regions to conduct outreach activities. The admin assistant must also be able to travel throughout the state and occasionally out of state to attend professional development statewide conferences when needed.   Posting Close Date: 09/18/2026   Open Until Filled: N/A   Minimum Qualifications EDUCATION: Bachelor's Degree EXPERIENCE: Four years experience in administrative staff work. OTHER: REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE/SKILLS/ABILITIES: Working knowledge of reference and research methods and techniques used in collecting, compiling, and organizing data and information, working knowledge of analytical and statistical principles and techniques. Skill in the use of office automation software and its applications, ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships, to handle sensitive materials with discretion and tact, to present ideas and information clearly and concisely, both orally and in writing; to perform mathematical computations; to present statistical material in chart and graph form. Ability to independently handle multiple tasks and set priorities. OTHER: Except for qualifications established by law, additional related experience and formal education in which one has gained the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for full performance of the work of the job class may be substituted for the education or experience requirement on a year-for-year basis with 30 college credits being equivalent to one year of experience. CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT: N/A Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Department VPR-UMCAPS-MD Small Business Development Ctr Worker Sub-Type Staff Contractual (C2) (Fixed Term) Salary Range $51,069.00 - $61,283.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Staff Contractual C2 benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Faculty-Specialist--Agricultural-Nutrient-Management-Program_JR104802": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist, Agricultural Nutrient Management Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: Position Summary/Purpose of Position: University of Maryland Extension (UME) seeks candidates for a 12-month professional-track Faculty Specialist position for the Agricultural Nutrient Management Program (ANMP) in the Agriculture and Food Systems (AgFS) Program. The ANMP Faculty Specialist has statewide responsibilities for creating and conducting training programs for farmers, private sector nutrient management plan writers, ANMP nutrient management advisors, and others. The ANMP Faculty Specialist teaches and supports farmers and nutrient management advisors in the development of nutrient management plans that balance nutrient inputs with crop requirements, thus optimizing production potential, improving farm profitability, reducing excess nutrient inputs into the Chesapeake Bay, and enabling producers to comply with Maryland’s Water Quality Improvement Act of 1998. Responsibilities: o Develop Extension guidance documents on agricultural nutrient management topics. o Lead development and instruction of in-person workshops: o Farmer Training and Certification, o How to Write a Nutrient Management Plan, o Fundamentals of Nutrient Management (UMD sections), and o Practical Experiences of Nutrient Management. o Assist farmers and private nutrient management consultants with development of their nutrient management plans remotely and through in-person update sessions. o Train new ANMP nutrient management advisors, mentor them to reach a proficiency in nutrient management plan writing, and provide professional development training on nutrient management topics. o Keep up to date with the latest related research through the scientific literature and attendance at regional and national conferences. o Learn to use and teach the nutrient management software. o Professional development to improve pedagogy. o Attend professional development programs to learn new pedagogy strategies and implement them in ANMP training programs. o Serve on and work collaboratively with UME teams to identify and develop statewide priorities and signature programs for nutrient management. o Serve on program, department, college, and university committees and boards as assigned. Qualifications: Required • Bachelor’s Degree in agronomy, crop science, soil science, or closely related field. • Work experience in agriculture, nutrient management, or closely related area. • Working knowledge of agriculture and farming issues. • Demonstrated teaching abilities. • Strong verbal and written communication skills. • Competency in the use of computer applications (e.g., Word, PowerPoint, Excel, GIS, Google Workspace). • Proven ability to work individually, as a member of a team, and lead a team. • Within one year of employment achieve certification through the Maryland Department of Agriculture as a Nutrient Management Consultant and maintain this certification. • Flexible working hours required; must be available for occasional evening and weekend programs. • A valid driver’s license and access to an automobile for travel. • Evidence of capacity to serve all Marylanders. • This position is subject to a Criminal History Record Check and University of Maryland Background check. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and clearance of the Criminal History Record Check. Preferences: • Master’s Degree in agronomy, crop science, soil science, or closely related field • Experience in agricultural planning. • Certification and experience as a Maryland nutrient management consultant. • Experience with distance education technology (e.g., Canvas, Blackboard) and pedagogy. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. • Nature of the Position: This position frequently presents information through vocal and written communication to individuals of various ages, socio-economic, and educational backgrounds. • Physical Demands: A routine part of this position's responsibilities would be to transport materials to and from teaching and event locations, including loading and unloading the vehicle. The employee will frequently lift and/or move items weighing up to 20 pounds. Set-up and teardown of displays, tables, and chairs would be necessary at many teaching sites. • Environmental: Team driven, office environment of professional character, competence, and collaboration. Deadline driven in terms of program planning and reporting. This position requires the employee to work outdoors at certain times of the year, especially during the time field research, demonstrations, and meetings are conducted as well as annual county fair. This may occur during very hot and/or inclement weather. • Visual Acuity: Visual acuity is required for preparing and analyzing written or computer data and presentations. Licenses/ Certifications: none Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: All applicants must apply online at UMD Jobs . A complete application packet includes a cover letter, resume, copies of transcripts, and three professional references, including name, mailing address, telephone number, and e-mail address.   Best Consideration Date: 9/27/2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-UME-Special Agriculture Programs Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $60,000 to $77,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Professor_JR104791": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Department of Art History and Archaeology at the University of Maryland College Park (UMCP) invites applications for an assistant professor of Early Modern European Art History (1300-1800). Topical and geographical specialty is open. We are particularly interested in scholars with research and teaching interests that complement the Department’s strengths in archaeology and cultural heritage, digital art history, the circulation of objects through trade or conquest, environmental humanities, and histories of race, representation, and colonial power. Candidates are invited to discuss their potential to engage the rich cultural resources of the Washington, D.C.-Maryland-Virginia area in their research and teaching. Successful candidates will demonstrate their readiness to contribute to our undergraduate major and M.A. and Ph.D. programs in Art History and Archaeology through classroom teaching and student mentorship.  Additional Job Details MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Applicants must have completed their doctoral degree in Art History or a related field when the term of appointment commences (July 1, 2027). Teaching experience at the college or university level is required. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS We seek candidates whose research, teaching, and service have prepared them to contribute to all the pillars of the College of Arts and Humanities’ Strategic Plan: Transformative Thinking; Boundless Creativity; Expansive Empathy; and Meaningful Futures. Contributions toward those goals and values might include leadership in teaching, mentoring, research, or service toward building an equitable and inclusive scholarly environment and/or increasing access or participation of all individuals equitably and fairly. REQUIRED APPLICATION MATERIALS (ONLINE): · 3-4-page letter of application (describing scholarly research agenda and teaching philosophy and experience, including proposed courses) · curriculum vitae · writing sample (one article or book/dissertation chapter) · contact information for three recommenders Best consideration date: 10/15/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Please direct questions to Holly Miller at hmmiller@umd.edu . The Department of Art History and Archaeology is a community of students and scholars that focuses on visual, material and textual expressions as means to understand culture. We critically engage with the reality of living in a world of images, working across a wide range of histories, perspectives and values. Our students at both the undergraduate and graduate levels learn from internationally recognized faculty experts in the field and engage with leading D.C. area arts institutions. Moreover, all students and faculty benefit from innovative technology and digital approaches through the Michelle Smith Collaboratory for Visual Culture.   Financial Disclosure Required For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ARHU-Art History & Archaeology Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $90,000 - $95,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Budget-Analyst_JR104805": {
      "title": "Budget Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organizational Summary Statement Position Overview and Key Responsibilities The University of Maryland is seeking a detail-oriented and highly analytical Budget Analyst to support the development, monitoring, analysis, and reporting of institutional budgets and financial activity. This position works collaboratively with academic and administrative units to provide accurate financial information, identify trends, support resource-planning decisions, and ensure compliance with university policies and applicable financial requirements. The Budget Analyst prepares budget and financial analyses, develops reports and forecasts, evaluates financial performance, and communicates findings and recommendations to university leadership and other stakeholders. This position also contributes to financial reconciliations, fiscal year-end activities, process improvements, and special projects. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong financial expertise, technological proficiency, sound judgment, initiative, and the ability to work effectively in a dynamic environment. About the University Budget Office at the University of Maryland The Budget Office coordinates the administration of the university’s budget for all university departments, with the primary objective of providing financial stability, ensuring the availability of required services, and maintaining a proper balance between the quality and cost of services. Physical Demands Sedentary Work: Primarily desk-based, requiring prolonged periods of sitting while performing tasks such as typing, filing, and using a computer. Repetitive Motion: Frequent use of a keyboard, mouse, and phone, which may involve repetitive hand and wrist movements. Occasional Lifting: Ability to lift and carry office materials, files, and supplies up to 20-25 pounds (e.g., boxes, office equipment). Standing and Walking: Occasional walking to meetings, interacting with staff or faculty, and attending departmental events or presentations. Visual and Mental Acuity: Requires the ability to focus on financial reports, spreadsheets, and documents for extended periods and manage multiple tasks simultaneously. Communication: Frequent verbal communication with staff, faculty, and campus administrators, requiring clear speech and the ability to hear and respond appropriately in meetings and discussions. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Five (5) years of professional budget, finance, or accounting experience. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of accounting systems, financial reporting, and budget preparation and analysis. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office and Google Suite products. Ability to multi-task and prioritize assignments. Ability to acquire, apply and expand knowledge of the University’s policies. Additional Job Details Preferences: Bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, business administration, economics, public administration, or a related field. Experience working in higher education, government, or another complex decentralized organization. Experience with Workday and Adaptive systems, data-visualization tools, and reporting applications. Knowledge of fund accounting, position budgeting, sponsored programs, or higher-education financial operations. Experience developing financial dashboards, automated reports, or advanced analytical models. Required Application Materials: Cover Letter, Resume, List of References   Best Consideration Date: N/A   Posting Close Date: September 11, 2026   Open Until Filled: No.   Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required Yes For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department VPF-University Budget Office Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $107,680.00 - $129,216.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/ART-HOUGHTON-JR-OFFICE-LAB/Extension-Program-Assistant--Forestry_JR104549": {
      "title": "Extension Program Assistant, Forestry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information Location: This position is located off-campus at the Wye Research & Education Center on the Eastern Shore in Queenstown, MD. Position Summary: The Forestry Extension Program within the University of Maryland Extension seeks a part-time Program Assistant to support research and education initiatives across Maryland. This role will assist with forest field data collection, coordination of workshops and events for key forest stakeholders, and written outreach (e.g., newsletters and Extension publications). The Program Assistant will interface regularly with UMD faculty and external partners statewide. Responsibilities: Collect and analyze ecological and silvicultural data in remote forest field locations across Maryland Apply technical expertise and knowledge in basic plant identification, plot sampling methods, and field safety protocols Perform technical duties to ensure rigorous data collection, data entry, and data cleaning/quality control to support the research and advising activities of the forestry program Assist and provide expertise for field operations and on-site field activities depending on experience and project needs Prepare educational literature , newsletters, promotional circulars, and program documents for distribution Support forestry faculty with technical duties to carry out teaching, demonstration, and educational outreach activities Assist in promoting and marketing educational programs, including coordinating logistics, outreach, registration, and materials setup/takedown for workshops, seminars, and field events Participate in the evaluation of the program by entering, organizing, and maintaining evaluation data Respond to oral and written requests for information, and attend or participate in conferences and partner meetings as needed Lead promotional and marketing efforts to recruit and register participants for forest landowner training courses Recruit, train, and serve as a primary point of contact for volunteer program leaders within the network Utilize automated systems and personal computers to develop and maintain database for volunteer communications, tracking, and relationship management Preferences: Bachelor’s degree in a related field. Experience with educational programming, event coordination, and/or workshop support Experience with volunteer management or community engagement First Aid/CPR certification FAA Part 107 certification (UAS/drone) Experience with RStudio and/or other statistical software Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Valid driver’s license and ability to travel to field sites and meetings as needed Demonstrated strong organizational skills, including the ability to manage work across multiple databases and workflows Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy and quality Proficiency with the Microsoft Office Suite (e.g., Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook) Ability to work in outdoor field settings, including: Ability to hike on uneven terrain Ability to lift and carry 25–40 lbs of field or event materials Additional Notes: The program is seeking a candidate who is eager to learn the basics of Maryland forest ecosystems and Extension programming. Fieldwork and event support may occur in variable outdoor conditions and may include occasional evening or weekend commitments depending on programming needs. Candidate must be eligible to work in the United States at the time of hiring. The department will not provide sponsorship for work visa requirements. Required Application Materials: N/A   Best Consideration Date: N/A   Posting Close Date: 09/11/2026   Open Until Filled: No   Minimum Qualifications EDUCATION: Graduation from High School (or GED) EXPERIENCE: Five years' experience performing a variety of duties in support of the teaching, demonstration, and advising work of Extension agents or in community outreach, health care, research, or social services programs. OTHER: A non-commercial Class C or equivalent driver's license valid in the State of Maryland. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE/SKILLS/ABILITIES: Working knowledge in the assigned area of specialization such as food and nutrition, housing, horticulture, soil nutrient management or youth programs. Skill to plan and carry out details of projects with general instruction. Skill to make arithmetic calculations, analyze data and draw conclusions. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Skill to establish and maintain successful working relationships. Ability to lift and transport supplies and equipment. Ability to operate manual and automated office equipment and personal computers. OTHER: Except for qualifications established by law, additional related experience and formal education in which one has gained the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for full performance of the work of the job class may be substituted for the education or experience requirement on a year-for-year basis with 30 college credits being equivalent to one year of experience. CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT: Employees in this job class are required to use their personal automobile while conducting official business. Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Department AGNR-UME-Wye REC Worker Sub-Type Staff Contractual (C2) (Fixed Term) Salary Range $45,375.00 - $54,450.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Staff Contractual C2 benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
