    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Post-Doctoral-Associate_JR104749": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Wilkinson lab at the University of Maryland, College Park, is hiring a postdoc to join an ongoing NIH-funded project titled “Social stress, epigenetic and immune function across the bat lifespans.” This project aims to determine if age, reproductive effort or social stress influence immune function and response across the lifespans of males and females from five different species of bats. The postdoc will be responsible for analyzing RNA and DNA methylation sequence data and will assist with sample collection from wild and captive bats. The postdoc will help plan, conduct, and publish research, contribute to the professional development of undergraduate and graduate students, and assist with data dissemination. Physical Demands: This position requires the individual to wear and work in personal protective equipment. This individual may be working with potential biohazards related to animal exposure (airborne allergens, contact reactions) and may be exposed to animal diseases. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in biology or related field is required by the start date of the appointment. Preferences: Candidates should have a strong background in bioinformatics, genomics and evolutionary biology. A track record of excellent written and verbal communication, and the ability to work well with others is required. Prior experience with analysis of DNA methylation is desirable. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Additional Job Details Interested candidates should apply through the University of Maryland job portal. Please feel free to email (wilkinso@umd.edu), with \"Post-doctoral position\" in the subject line, before applying to ask questions. This is a one-year appointment with potential for renewal for an additional year. Required Application Materials: 1) Cover letter describing research interests and motivation 2) CV 3) Names and email addresses for 3 references Best Consideration Date: 9/18/2026   Posting Close Date: Until Filled   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department CMNS-Biology Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $60,000 - $70,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Manager--Procurement-and-Travel_JR104807": {
      "title": "Manager, Procurement and Travel",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Institute for Advanced Computer Studies (UMIACS) is a multidisciplinary computing research institute led by distinguished researchers and supported by a cutting-edge infrastructure. UMIACS pioneers computational science involving national defense, precision medicine, big data, cybersecurity, language and culture, and more. As part of its operations, UMIACS purchases about $5M per year in travel, equipment, supplies, and a myriad other commodities and services to support our researchers. The Program Manager, Procurement and Travel performs a variety of professional administrative duties in support of the day‑to‑day operations of this work. Examples include: -Evaluating and honing institute procedures to ensure efficient operations as well as compliance with appropriate university, state and federal policies, procedures, and laws -Working with the technical and business staff members to maintain excellent customer service with respect to travel and procurement across different areas of the institute -Managing effort of multiple staff members who contribute to the completion of procurement and travel tasks -Serving as the subject matter expert on travel and procurement on state as well as federal funding sources -Ensuring that all travel and procurement tasks are executed correctly, in a timely manner, and that internal and external customers are kept abreast of important issues and timelines -Training new coordinators in procurement and travel work Physical Demands: This is an office job that requires the ability to be stationary for long periods time and the visual acuity and manual dexterity required to operate a computer and other standard office machinery. Must be able to attend meetings in various locations on campus. Licenses/Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Three (3) years of professional procurement experience. One (1) year leading or supervising professional staff. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of procurement policies and procedures, and federal, state, and other applicable related laws, rules, regulations, and ordinances. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office and Google Suite products. Ability to work on multiple projects and programs simultaneously. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Additional Job Details As this position deals with travel AND procurement, the three (3) years of professional experience may be in a combination of the two areas, not only procurement. Preferences: Experience on the UMD campus and/or with the Concur and/or Workday systems is highly preferred. Required Application Materials: a resume, cover letter, and list including the names and contact information for three professional references are required. Please ensure that all of these items are included before submitting your application.   Best Consideration Date: September 4, 2026   Open Until Filled: Yes   Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required Yes For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department CMNS-Institute for Advanced Computer Studies Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $98,800 - $105,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Graduate-Assistant_JR104806-1": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information Organizations Summary: The mission of the Research Development Office is to grow the volume and visibility of UMD’s research enterprise. We provide customized services to help faculty and faculty-led groups across the university turn ideas into action. Whether you are launching a new initiative, communicating a vision to university leaders, or identifying opportunities for unique research contributions, we are supportive partners during pivotal moments.  Job Summary: This is a 12-month, 20-hours-per-week full time graduate assistantship supporting the Research Development Office through data management, analytics, systems development, process improvement, and program support. We are seeking a motivated and proactive graduate student with strong technical, analytical, and organizational skills who is able to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. The position offers an opportunity to apply technical and analytical skills to strengthen the systems and processes that support research development programs and faculty funding activities. As a Graduate Assistant, you will work collaboratively with the Research Development team, with primary responsibilities focused on data systems, reporting, analytics, and workflow improvement. You will also develop familiarity with core Research Development programs and processes and provide backup programmatic and administrative support as needed. Data Systems & Management: Develop, maintain, and improve databases and other data systems that support Research Development programs, funding opportunities, reporting, and institutional knowledge. Dashboards, Analytics & Reporting: Develop and maintain dashboards, automated reports, visualizations, and other analytical tools to support program assessment, leadership reporting, strategic planning, and data-informed decision-making. Workflow Automation & Process Improvement: Identify opportunities to streamline processes and develop automated or technology-assisted workflows that reduce manual administrative work, improve data quality, and increase office efficiency. Systems & Tool Development: Support the development, testing, implementation, documentation, and ongoing maintenance of internal tools and resources, including data and reporting systems used across Research Development. Limited Submissions & Program Support: Develop and maintain working knowledge of limited submission competitions, internal funding programs, InfoReady, and associated application, deadline, and reporting processes. Serve as backup support for program administration and tracking as needed. Funding Opportunity Support: Assist the Research Development team in identifying, tracking, organizing, and communicating relevant federal, state, foundation, and corporate funding opportunities. Communication, Documentation & Outreach: Support documentation of systems and processes and assist, as needed, with communications, outreach materials, events, workshops, and other Research Development activities. Collaboration & Continuous Improvement: Work with Research Development staff to understand programmatic and operational needs, troubleshoot issues, and identify opportunities to improve how information, data, and technology are used across the office. Preferred Qualifications - While not required, the following qualifications would make candidates especially competitive: Enrollment as a graduate student at UMD (Master's or Ph.D. level). Demonstrated experience working with data, including organizing, cleaning, analyzing, and presenting information from multiple sources. Proficiency with Microsoft Excel, including advanced formulas, pivot tables, charts, and other data analysis and reporting functions. Experience with Python and the ability to understand, run, troubleshoot, and modify existing code used to support data processing, reporting, and workflow automation. Familiarity with GitHub or other version-control platforms for accessing, maintaining, and documenting code and technical projects. Experience with databases, automation, data systems, or other technical tools used to improve administrative and reporting workflows. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to understand a process or operational need and develop practical technical solutions. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate technical and non-technical information clearly to diverse audiences. Excellent organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively, learn new systems and technologies, and adapt to changing priorities. Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy, documentation, and quality control. Proficiency with common office and collaboration tools, including Microsoft Office and Google Workspace. Data Visualization & Dashboard Development: Experience developing interactive dashboards, reports, and visualizations using tools such as Power BI, Tableau, Looker Studio, or similar platforms. Database & Data Management: Experience designing, querying, maintaining, or integrating databases and structured data sources, including familiarity with SQL or similar tools. Automation & Systems Integration: Experience developing automated workflows, integrating data across systems, or using APIs and other tools to reduce manual processes and improve efficiency. Web & Application Development: Familiarity with HTML/CSS, JavaScript, or other web and application development technologies used to build or maintain internal tools and digital resources. AI-Assisted Tools & Workflows: Experience using or developing AI-assisted tools, applications, or workflows for data analysis, information management, process automation, or administrative support. Software Development Practices: Familiarity with software development practices, including version control, testing, documentation, and maintenance of existing code and technical projects. Data Analytics & Reporting: Experience analyzing complex data sets and developing reports or analytical products that support program assessment, strategic planning, or decision-making. Research Administration: Familiarity with research administration, sponsored research, research development, funding opportunities, or university administrative systems is a plus but not required. Appointment Continuity: Preference may be given to students who anticipate being eligible to hold the assistantship for two or more years. Physical Demands: Sedentary work performed in a normal office environment; exerts up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Ability to attend meetings both on and off campus. Spending long hours in front of a computer screen. Required Application Materials: Resume Cover Letter   Best Consideration Date: 09/09/2025 Posting Closing Date:  Open until filled Minimum Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Must be a registered graduate student in good standing enrolled in a degree program at the University of Maryland and must be making satisfactory progress toward the degree. Department VPR-Research Development Worker Sub-Type Graduate Assistant Salary Range $35958.00 - $37363.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Graduate Assistant benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Digitization-Services-Coordinator_JR104804": {
      "title": "Digitization Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: As the largest university library system in the Washington, D.C./Baltimore region, the University of Maryland (UMD) Libraries serve more than 41,000 students and 14,000 faculty and staff of the flagship College Park campus. Our extensive collections, innovative programs, and dynamic services enable student success, support teaching, research, and creativity, and enrich the intellectual and cultural life of our community. A member of the Big Ten Academic Alliance and the Association of Research Libraries, the UMD Libraries are nationally recognized for excellence in advancing the role of academic libraries. We are dedicated to fostering a welcoming and collaborative workplace where employees can grow, contribute their strengths, and be part of a community that advances discovery and learning. The Digitization Services Coordinator reports to the Head, Digital Collections and is a valued member of the of Digital Programs and Initiatives in the Digital Services and Technologies Division. The incumbent manages the in-house digitization operations at the University of Maryland Libraries in the Hornbake Digitization Center (HDC) - the central location in which most textual, photographic, and audio materials are digitized - and assists with outsourced digitization operations. The successful incumbent manages people, projects, vendor deliverables and estimates, and relationships with collections managers in coordination with the Head of Digital Collections. The Coordinator hires, trains, and supervises hourly student assistants to perform digitization work and quality control of all files and metadata. The individual manages and prioritizes short-term, user-initiated requests, and balances these with managing long-term projects. The Coordinator establishes quality assurance standards and manages quality control for all digital files and associated metadata records uploaded to all digital repositories. The individual provides oversight for digitization requests and projects, maintains digitization equipment, requests and negotiates quotes and purchase orders, and reports production and inspection statistics. The Coordinator maintains updated digitization and file management procedural documentation, and creates documentation and instructions for projects with the Head of Digital Collections. The Coordinator assesses digitization operation needs, is expected to remain current with evolving digitization standards and best practices, and will research development for expansion into additional formats Physical Demands:The position involves primarily sedentary work in an office setting with light to moderate noise. The position works in dusty environments; may require respiratory protection. Preferences: Education: Master’s degree in Library and Information Science from an ALA-accredited institution of higher education, or equivalent advanced degree in a relevant field can be substituted for two years of experience Experience: Four years of demonstrated digitization project management working in a cultural heritage institution or production management in a related field One year of supervisory experience Training or certificates in archives, preservation studies, digital curation, or special collections Continuing education in project management skills Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Experience with technology to retrieve, develop, and disseminate information products, services, and tools, e.g. project management tools Experience with hardware and software tools commonly used to digitize, inspect, post-process, and create deliverables Experience with a digital assets management system or digital repository Experience working with special collections and archival materials and their specialized care and handling Experience with identifying materials that warrant preservation Familiarity with various metadata standards and practices (schemas and thesauri) relevant to digital collections (e.g. MODS/METS, Dublin Core, PBCore, etc.) Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a flexible, production-based environment Demonstrated ability to handle analytical and detailed work Licenses/ Certifications: n'/a Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: One (1) year of professional experience in providing public library services or digitization services. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES:  Knowledge of digitization standards and workflows for various media. Knowledge of audiovisual born-digital materials and their digital conversion. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office and Google Workspace products. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Ability to multitask while demonstrating a commitment to customer service. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Resume Cover Letter 3 references with name, title, contact email, contact phone   Best Consideration Date: September 17, 2026   Posting Close Date: n/a   Open Until Filled: Yes   Job Risks Respiratory Protection Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department LIBR-Libraries Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $58,410 to $66,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Dining-Services-Specialist--Concessions_JR103802": {
      "title": "Food Service Specialist- Concessions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information Organizational Summary Statement: Under general supervision, functions as a specialist or entry level manager responsible for providing assistance in the planning and coordination of one or more components of a food service operation. Performs activities pertaining to food preparation and presentation, merchandising, calculation of food and labor costs, scheduling and employee relations. Assists in ensuring quality, cost efficient food preparation and the maintenance of safe and sanitary conditions. Preferences: ServSafe and TIPS certification preferred Licenses/ Certifications: Must have or obtain a driver’s license valid in Maryland with less than 5 points. Must have or obtain a Prince George’s County Maryland Health Department Food Service Manager Certification and TIPS (or equivalent certification) and State of Maryland Fire Marshall approved crowd management certification. All must be obtained within 90 days of hire and maintained throughout employment. After the job offer, but before hire, must pass a DOT physical and Drug Test arranged by the University and be able to maintain the DOT physical certification and pass random drug testing throughout employment. Physical Demands  This is an essential position and the incumbent must report to work when the campus is closed due to weather or other emergency situations. Must be able to work a variable schedule including weekends, nights, evenings, and holidays. Annual leave will not be granted for specific periods including the weeks preceding and right after the start of each semester, Football Weekends, Maryland Day, Family Weekend or special events. Must have the manual dexterity to operate equipment with or without accommodation and to lift up to 15 pounds regularly. The University of Maryland is a non-smoking campus. Must be able to lift 40 pounds on a regular basis and up to 75 pounds occasionally and stand, walk and work on feet for long periods of time. Must be able to work in extreme weather, humidity and temperature conditions including regularly working between 40 degrees and 90 degrees for extended periods and, from 15 below zero degrees to 40 degrees and from 90 degrees to 110 degrees for short periods of time.   Best Consideration Date: N/A   Posting Close Date: September 10, 2026   Open Until Filled: N/A   Minimum Qualifications EDUCATION: High School Diploma or GED. EXPERIENCE: Five years progressively responsible experience in commercial or institutional food service, two years of which must have been in a lead or supervisory capacity. OTHER: REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE/SKILLS/ABILITIES: Thorough knowledge and understanding of the principles and methods in large scale food preparation and service. Thorough knowledge of and skill in the application of procedures and standards of quality and quantity food selection, food preservation, food preparation, meal service, and portion control. Thorough knowledge of and skill in the use of food service equipment and materials. General knowledge of federal, state, and local health and sanitation regulations applicable to food service activities. Skill in providing guidance to food service personnel. Ability to organize and coordinate the work of food service operations and to control workload to assure quality service; to supervise and instruct food service personnel; to prepare and maintain records and reports; to communicate effectively both orally and in writing; to work in irritating environments and adverse temperature conditions; to lift, transport and stock food service supplies, materials and equipment. OTHER: Except for qualifications established by law, additional related experience and formal education in which one has gained the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for full performance of the work of the job class may be substituted for the education or experience requirement on a year-for-year basis with 30 college credits being equivalent to one year of experience. CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT: Candidates selected for employment may be subject to medical inquiries and/or medical examinations to determine ability to perform the job. Safe Food Handling and Sanitation Certification may be required. Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Department VPSA-DS-Concessions Worker Sub-Type Staff Contractual (C2) (Fixed Term) Salary Range $48,138.00 - $57,766.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Staff Contractual C2 benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/MT-Multi-Trades-Chief-I_JR104789": {
      "title": "MT Multi Trades Chief I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: To provide day-to-day liaison between occupants of assigned buildings and Facilities Management. To process and complete a wide range of multi-trade work orders. To be responsible for multiple buildings with unique needs, sophisticated mechanical and electrical equipment, laboratory and research areas, and high visibility buildings. The incumbent is generally responsible for 200,000 or more maintainable gross square footage. Physical Demands: Works around fixed machinery; works from ladders, aerial work platforms and scaffolding; manipulates heavy equipment and exerts force up to 70 pounds; works in hazardous or irritating environments; wears and works in personal protective equipment. Assigned work hours are 7:00 A.M.-3:30 P.M. Mon.-Fri. Incumbent is considered an Essential Employee (Catastrophic & Weather/Other); subject to a 24-hour day, 7-day week span of operation. Personal hand tools are not required for this position. If brought to the job, the University is not responsible for the repair or replacement of lost, stolen or damaged personal property. This position is ineligible for telework. Preferences: N/A Licenses/ Certifications: Must possess and maintain a Class C Driver’s license or equivalent valid in the State of Maryland with fewer than 6 points. Minimum Qualifications EDUCATION: EXPERIENCE: Four years progressively responsible experience in the trade(s) where assigned to include at least one year in a lead or supervisory capacity. In a Non-Supervisory/Leader position, 5 years of experience is required. OTHER: REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE/SKILLS/ABILITIES: Comprehensive knowledge of and skill in the methods and techniques of the trade(s) where assigned; of the OSHA regulations related to the trade(s) area. Thorough knowledge of and skill in the practical application of electronics, hydraulics, and mechanics as used in maintenance work; of basic mathematics including area, volume, weights and the practical application of fractions, percentages, ratios and proportions; of the care and storage of equipment and supplies used in the area where assigned. General knowledge of the principles of supervision in the maintenance trades. Skill in the use and maintenance of the tools and equipment of the trade(s) where assigned. Ability to read, interpret, and work from blueprints, schematics, drawings, and specifications; to communicate effectively both orally and in writing; to lead and train skilled and unskilled employees in assigned trade(s) work; to prepare summaries and reports; to work in, on, around, over and under fixed equipment and machinery; to work from ladders and scaffolding; to manipulate heavy equipment, tools, and supplies and/or exert force up to 70 lbs.; to concurrently manipulate multiple controls on machinery and equipment; to work in hazardous or irritating environments, confined spaces, and adverse weather or temperature conditions; to wear and work in personal protective equipment. OTHER: Except for qualifications established by law, additional related experience and formal education in which one has gained the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for full performance of the work of the job class may be substituted for the education or experience requirement on a year-for-year basis with 30 college credits being equivalent to one year of experience. CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT: Candidates selected for employment may be subject to medical inquiries and/or medical examinations to determine ability to perform the job. A non-commercial Class C or equivalent driver's license may be required. Employees in this job class may be required to be trained to work with asbestos. Employees in this job class assigned to work with equipment containing CFC refrigerants must achieve and maintain valid certification in accordance with federal law. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: N/A Best Consideration Date: N/A Posting Close Date:  September 9, 2026 Open Until Filled: No Visa Requirement: **This position does not provide sponsorship for Visa** Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department VPA-FM-O&M-Area Maintenance Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $49,582.00 - $59,498.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Nonexempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
