    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/SARE-Business-Manager_JR103785": {
      "title": "SARE Business Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information Job Description Summary : Sustainable Agriculture Research and Education (SARE) invites applications for a 12-month, renewable, full-time Business Manager, to work with its National Reporting, Coordinating, and Communications Office (NRCCO) located in College Park, Md. SARE is a program of the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) National Institute of Food and Agriculture (NIFA) that offers farmer-driven, grassroots grants and education programs. SARE’s NRCCO operates under cooperative agreements from the USDA through the University of Maryland (UMD) in its College of Agriculture and Natural Resources’ Maryland Agricultural Experiment Station. More information can be found at: https://www.sare.org/ .  The NRCCO is primarily responsible for creating nationally focused print and digital technical guides and educational resources for farmers, ranchers, and agricultural service providers, and managing the distribution and sale of these materials. Additionally, the NRCCO supports SARE's regional grant and outreach programs by directing national program efforts and providing opportunities for cross-regional information sharing. This support includes maintaining a digital grant management system, developing the SARE websites, providing communication resources, and coordinating national SARE workshops and outreach initiatives.  The Business Manager will directly support the SARE Associate Director in overseeing the administrative responsibilities associated with the functions of the NRCCO. Typically, this includes managing five 5-year cooperative agreements (approx. $1.5M to $2.0M each), about 50 supplier/subaward/employee/service contracts, material distribution, 2 to 3 national in-person workshops, and assisting with 2 to 3 virtual meetings, annually. Occasionally, the NRCCO also manages special projects and national SARE initiatives. The Business Manager will also ensure that NRCCO activities and resources comply with USDA NIFA and university procedures through engagement with the UMD College of Agriculture and Natural Resources. This position provides ample opportunities to engage with UMD and NRCCO colleagues and other national partners, who enthusiastically support sustainable agriculture, farms, and ranches. This role requires annual out-of-state travel.  Overall, the Business Manager will enhance the efficiency and effectiveness for which the NRCCO manages its administrative activities in support of its program efforts. This position reports to the SARE Associate Director at UMD and requires collaboration and frequent communication with NRCCO and UMD colleagues and SARE national partners. Preferred Qualifications : Experience with university education and outreach programs.  Familiarity with UMD administrative offices, procedures and data systems.  Familiarity or experience working with USDA grants and contracts. Experience making travel plans within the U.S. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities : Administrative expertise : Broad administrative skill set, including experience with database management systems to maintain records and generate reports. Strong organizational and time management skills: Demonstrated ability to independently organize and prioritize tasks and handle complex administrative and clerical duties efficiently and in a timely manner. Excellent attention to detail, strong problem-solving skills, and a positive attitude. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills: Proven ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing, including composing and editing correspondence or reports. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to navigate sensitive issues with discretion and professionalism. Technical proficiency: Intermediate proficiency in various computer software packages, and experience working in shared cloud-based work spaces, digital meeting platforms, and various database systems.  Strong work ethic: Demonstrated ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions, with a commitment to meeting deadlines, achieving high-quality results, and a desire to learn new things.  Customer service orientation: Strong interpersonal skills with an ability to build and maintain strong relationships with colleagues, partners and stakeholders, providing excellent customer service. Ability to work effectively in a semi-remote, collaborative team-based environment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities : Contract & Budget Management Serves as the main point of support for SARE business operations at UMD to the NRCCO’s Associate Director by managing multiple program budgets (annual, 5-year USDA NIFA cooperative agreements), accounts, contracts, expenditures, and reconciliations. Administers purchase orders, subawards, and contracts in accordance with UMD policies and USDA requirements for records, reports, and conditions for expenditure of funds - including communicating with contracted suppliers as needed. Assists with the print production process and managing SARE publication fulfillment services including communicating with vendors of print projects, monitoring inventory, coordinating book orders, processing checks, and distributing free materials. Organizes and leads regular NRCCO budget meetings to discuss program activities and analyze project spending reports. Meeting and Workshop Administration Supports the NRCCO Associate Director by arranging travel and assisting with coordinating logistics for national in-person SARE meetings or workshops. Processes travel requests and manages associated meeting or workshop expenses, in accordance with USDA and UMD policies and requirements. Travels to approximately two out of state, multi-day meetings or workshops per year. Other Responsibilities Contributes to managing and developing SARE NRCCO’s shared information and reference resources. Engage with NRCCO, UMD and national SARE groups and individuals with timely responses via email, instant message, and phone correspondence. Provides occasional administrative assistance with USDA contracts and hiring. Physical Demands : Sedentary work. The employee will frequently lift and/or move items weighing up to 20 pounds. Set up and teardown of research machinery, project displays, tables, and chairs may be necessary at workshops.  Additional Job Details : Required Application Materials: Resume Cover Letter Names and contact information for three professional references   Best Consideration Date: August 28, 2026   Open Until Filled: Yes Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Three (3) years of professional human resources, payroll, finance, accounting, procurement, or travel coordination experience. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES: Knowledge of human resources policies and procedures, and federal, state, and other applicable human resources related laws, rules, regulations, and ordinances. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office products. Ability to multi-task and prioritize assignments. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Department AGNR-AES-Agriculture Experiment Station-Associate Dir. Worker Sub-Type Staff Contractual (C2) (Fixed Term) Salary Range $74611-$89533 Benefits Summary For more information on Staff Contractual CII benefits, select this link   . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Intellectual-Property-Associate_JR104648": {
      "title": "Intellectual Property Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organizational Summary: UM Ventures, College Park accelerates knowledge creation and dissemination that can scale the impact of UMD research by transforming laboratory discoveries into products and services that deliver economic and societal benefit. In its mission to scale UMD impact, UM Ventures, College Park leverages a variety of services and resources for faculty, staff, and students to protect intellectual property resources, build partnerships with business and government, and return investment to the University and its stakeholders through technology licensing and forming startups. From the laboratory to the marketplace, UM Ventures, College Park provides end-to-end support for researchers, entrepreneurs, and industry partners. Job Description Summary: UM Ventures provides in-house technology commercialization capability to complement the research administrative support services provided to the University's research community. The Intellectual Property (IP) Associate is responsible for maintaining appropriate intellectual property protection by: reviewing invention disclosure information, drafting and preparing various administrative and IP related documentation, and monitoring the database for accuracy and integrity so deadlines are satisfied. The Intellectual Property Associate reports to the Assistant Director, Operations. Physical Demands: Sedentary work performed in a normal office environment; exerts up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Ability to attend meetings both on and off campus. Spending long hours in front of a computer screen. Licenses/Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. \n \nExperience: One (1) year of professional experience drafting, editing, and preparing patent prosecution documents.\n \nOther: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. Knowledge of federal intellectual property law and policies.\nKnowledge of procedures and regulations of the patent prosecution process.\nSkill in oral and written communication.\nSkill in the use of Microsoft Office products. \nAbility to work on multiple projects and programs simultaneously.\nAbility to conduct research and analysis for aid program development.\nAbility to analyze data and provide insight and recommendations to stakeholders.\nAbility to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Resume, cover letter, list of references, & unoffical transcripts   Best Consideration Date: 08/21/26 Open Until Filled: Y   Job Risks Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department VPR-EconDev-UM Ventures, College Park Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $77,918.00 to $93501.60 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Videographer-and-Editor_JR104619-1": {
      "title": "Videographer and Editor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Videographer and Editor will play a key role in creating visual stories that support the University of Maryland's strategic mission and advance institutional objectives. The Office of Marketing and Communications produces a wide range of branded content, commercials, mini-docs, promotional and fundraising videos, social media content, and live events. The Videographer and Editor is a creative and technical role that requires audio-video storytelling, motion graphics expertise and field production skills. They must have an excellent creative eye, the ability to tell engaging stories, and an understanding of modern editing techniques, styles and trends. We are looking for a self-starter who can bring enthusiasm and new ideas for content creation. Although most work will happen during business hours, this position may need to help with last minute updates to make publication deadlines or to cover after-hours events like Commencement. Responsibilities include: Video Editing Apply various methods of post-production creative editing to complete long and short form video projects. Complete understanding of the video production process to include a familiarity of conceptualizing, scripting, filming and editing. Video editing using Adobe Premiere Pro. Color correct video footage using Premiere or other color grading software. Design motion graphics and other effects using After Effects and Photoshop. Assist with captions, thumbnail development and other aspects to increase impact. Manage storage and archiving of footage and projects, including detailed metadata. Supervise and provide maintenance of video editing hardware and software. Videography Produce video content for numerous platforms including the web, social media, and television by collecting clean audio (both interviews and natural sound), compelling high-quality video and memorable moments. Complete tasks as needed and assigned in all areas of field production to include: idea development, site surveys, location scouting, equipment transportation, set up audio, lighting, and cameras. Conduct interviews in the field. Cover events and capture general campus B-roll. Ability to work solo and on a team in the field. Project Management/Office Duties Assist in all aspects of video production including supporting file management. Perform general office support including updates to the project management system and making inventory orders. Coordinate with campus partners and outside vendors. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Three (3) years of experience in related field. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year-for-year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education.   KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of organizational principles and time management practices. Skill in project management, including planning, coordinating, tracking progress, and ensuring successful completion of initiatives within established timelines. Skill in verbal and written communication to clearly convey information, prepare correspondence, and interact effectively with diverse stakeholders. Ability to analyze complex information, identify issues, and evaluate options. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision. Ability to maintain a high level of attention to detail. Additional Job Details Preferences: N/A Physical Demands: This position requires the ability to carry and transport heavy camera equipment across campus locations. Ability to move from location to location quickly, either by foot or by vehicle. Required Application Materials: Resume, Cover Letter, List of 3 Professional References Best Consideration Date: September 2nd, 2026 Posting Close Date: N/A Open Until Filled: Yes   Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department PRES-Office of Marketing and Communications Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $79,200 - $86,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
