    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Professor---Associate-Dean_JR104541": {
      "title": "Professor & Associate Dean",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization Summary Statement Professor and Associate Dean for Academic Programs and Faculty Affairs College of Agriculture and Natural Resources University of Maryland, College Park The College of Agriculture and Natural Resources at the University of Maryland, College Park, invites applications and nominations for the position of Professor and Associate Dean for Academic Programs and Faculty Affairs. The University of Maryland is a Land-Grant Institution, a Sea Grant Institution, a Carnegie Research Extensive University, and a flagship of the state University System of Maryland. The University has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and extension. Degree programs in the College are offered in Agricultural and Resources Economics, Animal and Avian Sciences, Environmental Science and Technology, Environmental Science and Policy, Nutrition and Food Science, and Plant Science and Landscape Architecture, as well as a two-year certificate program in the Institute of Applied Agriculture. The college also offers M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Veterinary Medicine. Currently, the college enrollment includes 1100 undergraduates, approximately 300 graduate students seeking M.S. or Ph.D. degrees, and 120 students in the Institute of Applied Agriculture. The College has 292 faculty FTEs and 305 staff, on- and off-campus. University of Maryland Extension has 24 county/city offices located throughout the state and is jointly administered with the University of Maryland Eastern Shore, our 1890 Land-Grant partner. The Maryland Agricultural Experiment Station has 8 statewide research facilities. Additional information about the College is available at its website: www.agnr.umd.edu. Through its associate deans, the College of Agriculture and Natural Resources fosters a close collaborative working relationship between instruction, research, and extension activities. Position Description The Associate Dean is responsible to the Dean of the College for meeting the mission and goals of the college’s undergraduate instructional programs. In addition, the Associate Dean undertakes faculty affairs responsibilities, which involve coordinating policies and procedures related to college and departmental tenure and promotion, mentoring faculty, and resolving faculty issues. The Associate Dean interacts extensively with the Associate Provost and the Dean for Undergraduate Studies, and develops connections and collaborations with other colleges on campus, as well as two- and four-year colleges throughout the state of Maryland. Responsibilities: The Associate Dean oversees all undergraduate and certificate programs in the college’s six departments and the institute associated with it. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to the following: Provide leadership for the coordination and facilitation of recruitment, retention, and success of  undergraduate students. Provide visionary leadership by establishing priorities for the undergraduate educational program development in collaboration with college departments and programs. Ensure the quality and integrity of learning outcomes assessments across degree programs. Spearhead curricular review and revitalization efforts and support teaching and learning activities. Actively participate and represent college interests on university curriculum and education committees for undergraduate programs. Provide oversight of academic programs’ annual budget and allocation of teaching assistantships to AGNR departments in support of university general education programs. Provide program coordination for undergraduate research, study abroad, and internship activities. Provide leadership in the planning and implementation of college-wide academic activities. Assist the college efforts to increase scholarship aid through gifts Work with departments and the college to improve and innovate capacity, such as distance education. Represent the college statewide on all issues related to undergraduate education. Coordinate faculty affairs policy/procedures relating to college and departmental APT and AEP guidelines, mentoring process for both tenure-track and professional-track faculty, post-tenure review, and other items related to the area of faculty affairs. Provide input and leadership to the college’s efforts to facilitate improved alumni and public relations efforts. Provide leadership to advance connections with alumni through collaborative initiatives with the Office of External Relations that promote engagement, philanthropy, mentorship, and lifelong involvement with the college. Advance strategic partnerships with industry and UMD Career Services to create innovative opportunities that prepare students for successful careers through internships, mentorship, experiential learning, and employer engagement. Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate in a discipline related to one of the academic departments in the college. The credentials to be appointed to the rank of professor with tenure in one of the College’s academic departments. Demonstrated leadership abilities and proven management skills to work effectively with students, staff and faculty, along with skills to direct office staff that supports academic programs. Demonstrated commitment to academic excellence. Excellence in instruction and advising. Experience and professional interest in administering, planning, and implementing academic programs. An understanding of the role of education in the context of a land-grant institution. Outstanding communication and advocacy skills. Ability to manage budget priorities and balance diverse office needs. Salary / Benefits: Salary will be commensurate with experience of the candidates. The University of Maryland offers an extensive benefits package. Additional Job Details Applications: Best consideration will be given to applications received by September 15, 2026; however, the search will continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a complete curriculum vitae, the names, addresses, telephone numbers, fax numbers, and e-mail of five professional references, and a letter of interest. It is recommended within your letter of interest that you highlight your thoughts about advancing the College’s Academic Programs and provide brief examples of leadership successes that are not evident in your CV. Applications and nominations should be addressed to Dr. Puneet Srivastava, Chair, Search Committee, Office of the Dean, University of Maryland, 1296 Symons Hall, College Park, MD 20742. An electronic application is required and must be submitted through UMD Jobs . Applications will be kept confidential. The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. EEO Statement   Financial Disclosure Required Yes For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-College of Agriculture & Natural Resources Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $149,000-$254,811 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Ongoing-Care-Team-Clinician_JR104583": {
      "title": "Ongoing Care Team Clinician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Ongoing Care Team (OCT) Clinician is responsible for providing services to students and the University community, by offering individual and group psychotherapy/counseling, diagnostic assessment, psychological and career testing, consultation, outreach, and crisis intervention. The OCT Clinician is skilled in fostering the mental health, academic progress and career development of University students through a variety of psychotherapeutic and psycho-educational interventions. Physical Demands: Standard office work. Minimum Qualifications To be eligible for hire as a Staff Psychologist (exempt salaried 4): Education: Doctoral degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Five (5) years of clinical practice in total, including experience gained throughout the Educational training. Licenses/ Certifications: Licensed or license-eligible to practice psychology in the State of Maryland within 1 year from hire. To be eligible for hire as a Counselor (exempt salaried 2): Education: Master’s degree from an accredited college or university.  Experience: Two (2) years of clinical experience in an ambulatory mental health setting. Licenses/ Certifications: Licensed or license-eligible as a mental health provider in the State of Maryland. Other: Licensed Graduate Professional Counselor (LGPC) may also be considered with at least 2000 hours of post-graduate supervised clinical work and the ability to obtain a Licensed Certified Social Worker-Clinical (LCSW-C) or Licensed Clinical Professional Counselor (LCPC) license within one year. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of individual and group psychotherapy, counseling, diagnostic assessment, psychological and career testing, consultation, outreach, and crisis intervention. Knowledge of group psychodynamics and supervision. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office products.  Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Additional Job Details Preferences: n/a Required Application Materials: Resume, Cover Letter and List of References Best Consideration Date: 09/2/2026 Posting Close Date: N/A Open Until Filled: Yes Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department VPSA-Counseling Center Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range 84,500 - 100,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
