    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/AV-Specialist--AV-Systems-and-Classroom-Support_JR104558": {
      "title": "AV Specialist, AV Systems and Classroom Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organizational Summary Statement: This position is available within the University of Maryland’s Division of Information Technology (DIT). The AV Specialist works within the Academic Technology & Innovation team to drive learning innovations through institutional-wide initiatives. This individual will work directly with the campus community to support classroom technology and facilitate AV operations in formal and informal learning spaces. The AV Specialist reports to the Assistant Manager of AV Systems and Classroom Support, who assists in managing the operations and maintenance of approximately 335 instructional technology classrooms. The specialist is responsible for assisting faculty users and local department staff with instructional technology infrastructure. This position provides technical support that ensures the proper operation, maintenance, monitoring, testing and repair of complex networked AV equipment and control systems. The specialist will also be required to troubleshoot Crestron control processors, touch panels, routers, audio DSPs (Crestron and others) and Crestron peripherals to support instructional technology classrooms. The Specialist will also review requirements and design classroom AV systems, build/install new classroom AV systems, perform tests and pilot installations of viable technologies. The Specialist will produce needed documentation. **This position is considered essential and may be required to work at the normal work location or an alternative location during a major catastrophic event, weather emergency, or other operational emergency to help maintain the continuity of University services.** **May be required to work evenings, nights, weekends, or different shifts for extended periods.** Physical Demands: Must be able to operate test equipment, machinery and AV equipment; use power tools; work at heights using ladders and scaffolding; and drive a motor vehicle. Must be able to perform extensive standing, driving, walking and climbing; to lift up to 50 lbs.; to manipulate up to 100 lbs. with assistance; to transport and stock assigned supplies and materials; to wear personal protective equipment. Must be able to bend, stoop and climb to reach materials (must be able to climb a ladder and to work from a lift up to twenty feet in height). Licenses/Certifications: Must possess a valid drivers license Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Three (3) years of audio visual system experience. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of audio visual systems and equipment. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office and Google Workspace products. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Ability to multitask while demonstrating a commitment to customer service. Additional Job Details Preferences: Proficient with rack fabrication & wiring. Strong understanding of signal flow, signal formats, & transportation protocols.  Crestron configuration knowledge, along with their software suite.  Audio DSP knowledge (QSys & Biamp). Wireless microphone systems knowledge. AV system commissioning knowledge EDID & HDCP knowledge. Networking for AVoIP, Dante, AES67, NDI, etc knowledge. General Networking knowledge. AVIXA CTS & other industry certifications. High level of energy, drive, enthusiasm, initiative, creativity and commitment. Ability to work in a busy environment with multiple project timelines and on own initiative, be self-motivated and flexible  Committed to customer satisfaction: exceptional skills in collaboration, consultation, communication, customer support, data analysis, and time management.   Additional Information:  Please note that all positions within the Division of Information Technology (DIT) have an in person component with expected time in our College Park, MD location per week. Telework is not a guaranteed work arrangement.   Visa Sponsorship Information: DIT will not sponsor the successful candidate for work authorization in the United States now or in the future. F1 STEM OPT support is not available for this position . Remote Work:  This position may be eligible for some telework, but that will be dependent on projects and needs of the project/department. There will be a regular in-office requirement. Required Application Materials: Resume  Cover Letter List of three Reference s Best Consideration Date: 08/21/2026 Posting Close Date: Open until filled Open Until Filled: Yes Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department DIT-ATI-Learning Technology Strategy (LTS) Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $75,840.00 - $91,008.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Sustainable-Agriculture-Program-Manager_JR103786": {
      "title": "Sustainable Agriculture Program Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information Job Description Summary : Sustainable Agriculture Research and Education (SARE) invites applications for a 12-month, renewable, full-time Program Manager to work with its National Reporting, Coordinating, and Communications Office (NRCCO) located in College Park, Md. SARE is a program of the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) National Institute of Food and Agriculture (NIFA) that offers farmer-driven, grassroots grants and education programs. SARE’s NRCCO operates under cooperative agreements from the USDA through the University of Maryland (UMD) in its College of Agriculture and Natural Resources’ Maryland Agricultural Experiment Station. More information can be found at: https://www.sare.org/ .  The NRCCO is primarily responsible for creating and managing the distribution of print and digital technical guides and educational resources for U.S. farmers, ranchers, and agricultural service providers. The office manages five ongoing work plans simultaneously, typically completing around 8 to 10 written and digital outreach products focused on various topics within Sustainable Agriculture, annually. Additionally, the NRCCO supports SARE's regional grant and outreach programs by directing national program efforts and providing opportunities for cross-regional information sharing among its partners. This support includes maintaining a digital grant management system, developing the SARE websites, providing communication resources, and coordinating national SARE workshops, program meetings, and outreach initiatives.  The Program Manager will be a key member of a collaborative, supportive team, responsible for developing written and digital educational and outreach resources focused on various sustainable agriculture topics. This role also involves assisting to develop promotion plans, write press releases, and identify effective outreach channels and new educational formats. Additionally, the Program Manager will assist with creating engaging online and in-person educational opportunities for national SARE partners and stakeholders. These include contributions to programs like SARE Fellows and National Continuing Education, as well as occasional workshops, conferences, or meetings. This position provides ample opportunities to engage with NRCCO colleagues and other national partners, who enthusiastically support sustainable agriculture, farms, and ranches. The role requires annual out-of-state travel.  Overall, the Program Manager will provide a creative and professional perspective to sustainable agriculture outreach while balancing daily operational tasks and long-term program objectives. This position reports to the SARE Associate Director at UMD and requires collaboration and frequent communication with NRCCO and UMD colleagues and national SARE partners. Preferred Qualifications : M.S. in sustainable agriculture, natural resource conservation, agriculture education, or related fields.  Experience with agriculture outreach programing or Cooperative Extension.  Previous experience maintaining website content and using various design and editing software like: Adobe Creative Suite, InDesign, Photoshop, Bridge, Illustrator, and Wordpress. Familiarity with publication and photo management and/or digital accessibility? Knowledge, Skills and Abilities : Excellent communication and interpersonal skills: Proven ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing, including composing and editing educational resources (written, in-person, digital, and/or video) across various topics in sustainable agriculture, with a focus on plain language principles and practical information sharing.  Strong facilitation and organizational skills: Experience planning educational engagements and leading discussions (in-person and virtual). Technical proficiency: Intermediate proficiency with various computer software packages, and experience working in shared cloud-based work spaces, digital meeting platforms, and various database systems.  Strong organizational and time management skills: Ability to independently organize, and prioritize tasks, handling multiple projects and duties efficiently and with flexibility. Excellent attention to detail, strong problem-solving skills, and a positive attitude. Strong work ethic: Demonstrated ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions, with a commitment to meeting deadlines, achieving high-quality results, and a desire to learn new things.  Customer service orientation: Strong interpersonal skills with an ability to build and maintain strong relationships with colleagues, partners and stakeholders, providing excellent customer service. Ability to work effectively in a semi-remote, collaborative team-based environment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities : Content Development and Distribution Contributes significantly to the production of all print and digital media projects (e.g., books, bulletins, promotional materials, web pages, press releases) from start to finish, including managing the print production process.  Leads the team in researching and identifying best avenues for outreach and communications. Advises staff on how social media and/or new and notable outreach and communication strategies, including artificial intelligence (AI) programs, can be used to advance the NRCCO’s mission. Interfaces with the NRCCO team to ensure timely development, design, and editing/proofreading of print and online digital content prior to being publicly available. Collaborates with the NRCCO team and national SARE Outreach Steering Committee to select and develop content for publications, digital media, and other educational resources. Meeting and Workshop Coordination Co-develops and delivers engaging educational opportunities at in-person and online programs for national SARE partners and stakeholders (e.g., SARE Fellows Program, SARE Outreach Steering Committee). Assists with planning, facilitating logistics and communication with any guest speakers, organizing technology resources, developing and distributing materials, and other tasks associated with workshops and meetings in-person or virtual events. Provides logistical support at in-person and virtual events, including note taking. Collaboration and Team Responsibilities Travel to 1 to 3 out-of-state, multi-day trips per year.  Contributes to managing and developing SARE NRCCO’s shared information and reference resources.  Engage with NRCCO, UMD and national SARE groups and individuals with timely responses via email, instant message, and phone correspondence. Physical Demands of Position : Sedentary work. The employee will frequently lift and/or move items weighing up to 20 pounds. Set up and teardown of research machinery, project displays, tables, and chairs may be necessary at workshops.  Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Resume Cover Letter Names and contact information for three professional references 1-2 pages of professional and/or creative writing samples. Best Consideration Date: August 28, 2026 Open Until Filled: Yes   Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Three (3) years of professional program management or higher education experience. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of business acumen to understand key business drivers, organizational communications, and data. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office products. Ability to exercise independent judgment and discretion. Ability to develop and administer new policies and procedures. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Department AGNR-AES-Agriculture Experiment Station-Associate Dir. Worker Sub-Type Staff Contractual (C2) (Fixed Term) Salary Range $82,000 - $87,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Staff Contractual CII benefits, select this link   . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Professor_JR104554": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary ORGANIZATION'S SUMMARY STATEMENT: The Department of Kinesiology within the School of Public Health at the University of Maryland College Park (https://sph.umd.edu/academics/departments-units/department-kinesiology) invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The department is seeking a highly motivated and collaborative scientist in the area of biomechanics. Applicants for this position should have strong potential for research excellence in the understanding of mechanical, neuromuscular, and/or computational mechanisms underlying human movement across the lifespan. Applicants with research foci in the areas of musculoskeletal biomechanics, neuromechanics, injury and rehabilitation, wearable sensing, movement analytics, and/or biomechanics of aging and disease are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and sustain a high-quality, extramurally funded research program, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in biomechanics and related areas, advise and mentor graduate students, and serve on comprehensive examination committees and department committees. Special consideration will be given to candidates who complement ongoing research within the department. PURPOSE OF POSITION: The Department of Kinesiology embodies the core pillars of the University of Maryland’s Strategic Plan by advancing innovative research, reimagining learning, and addressing grand challenges in human health and performance. The department examines the complex role of physical activity and movement in health and well-being across the lifespan through interdisciplinary collaboration and research. The University of Maryland is the flagship institution of the state of Maryland on the ancestral lands of the Piscataway people, the traditional stewards of the lands where we work, live, and learn. The University of Maryland is an extraordinary place—vibrant and dynamic and diverse. We are a place of learning: a school dedicated to the art and science of education and committed to reimagining teaching and learning inside both classrooms and communities. We are a campus dedicated to the indisputable value of science and humanities, inquiry, and creativity, and comprising thousands of researchers and discoverers working in hundreds of laboratories, libraries, and collaborative spaces. Strategically located just a few miles from the US capital, our university is a place where new knowledge is pursued, discovered, and championed. We are also a community, nearly half a million members strong, of diverse students, faculty, staff, and alumni; a small city of residents and commuters, first responders and health care workers, learners, artists, and athletes; a place where thousands come to work every day to make a difference. Our diversity is integral to our excellence. And, ours is a community that is intrinsically connected to our surrounding neighborhoods and our state, our nation, and our world. The University of Maryland remains, since our founding, an institution of change and progress dedicated to the public good. Our university is evolving faster than at any moment in its storied history. Our guiding principles are helping us to empower the next generation of leaders, educators, scientists, and global citizens to develop creative solutions to the grand challenges of our times. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Candidates should possess a doctoral degree in kinesiology, biomechanics, biomedical engineering, mechanical engineering, exercise science, or a closely related field. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Demonstrated expertise in the biomechanics of human movement. Evidence of (or demonstrated potential for) a sustainable and focused research program. Evidence of experience with advanced laboratory (clinical, basic, biomechanical, or computational) methodologies Evidence of (or demonstrated potential for) a strong publication record in kinesiology. Evidence of (or demonstrated potential for) high-quality teaching and mentoring in kinesiology. Evidence of strong communication, collaboration, and leadership skills within a research team. Preferences: Postdoctoral research experience is strongly preferred. There should be evidence of the potential to obtain extramural funding. Evidence of classroom teaching experience and research mentoring is desirable. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: No unusual physical or environmental demands Normal classroom teaching demands Using a computer and keyboard Sitting for periods of time Standing for periods of time Using lab or mechanical equipment LICENSES/CERTIFICATIONS: N/A Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover letter describing interests, qualifications, and current research Curriculum vitae Three representative publications that are illustrative of their research expertise List of three references (letters not required at time of application) Applications will be held in confidence until finalists are invited for campus interviews. References will not be contacted without a candidate’s consent.   Review of applications will begin on October 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Best Consideration Date: 10/16/2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department SPHL-Kinesiology Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $100,000-$110,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Corporate-Relations-Coordinator--Part-time-_JR103907-1": {
      "title": "Corporate Relations Coordinator (Part-time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Department of Computer Science is top-ranked for research and teaching, with its undergraduate computer science program ranked 9th among public universities by U.S. News & World Report. The undergraduate program currently educates over 4,000 students from around the world. The graduate program ranks 16th in the nation (9th among public institutions), with over 400 graduate students enrolled. Our faculty have been recognized with memberships in the National Academy of Engineering, fellowships in professional scientific organizations including ACM and IEEE, NSF Faculty Early Career Development awards and Sloan Fellowships. Position Summary: As a member of the External Relations team, under the supervision of the Director of Corporate Partnership Development, this position will be responsible for contributing as needed to the successful completion of projects and events for the Corporate Partners in Computing (CPIC) program and other external relations activities. This position plays an integral role in supporting the team's activities, including planning and executing corporate sponsored career/internship recruiting events, managing CPIC member services, coordinating research meetings with industry, and collaborating with senior administrators on various tasks. Due to the nature of the work, this position requires the ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends, on a regular basis. Specific responsibilities include: Plans and executes corporate student events, speaker series, and other events targeted to students for CPIC. Supports and stewards corporate partnerships by preparing proposals and invoices for prospective and current partners, tracks CPIC member activities, and coordinates industry partner on-campus meetings. Supports funding efforts for student groups, faculty and CPIC. Prepares written briefings related to prospective companies, CPIC's year-end reports, and other CPIC related reports and newsletters. Sources information and produces a student-facing weekly announcement of corporate and relevant department events for CPIC. Additionally, produces a monthly newsletter for CPIC partners which highlights department events and news. Physical Demands: Work takes place in both an office environment and in on-campus buildings. Must be able to sit for extended periods of time performing general office functions with periods of standing for event setup, registration, and event supervision. Must be able to walk, bend, stoop, kneel, climb stairs, push and reach with arms. Ability to lift and carry items up to 25 lbs. and arrange furniture for events. Will be required to attend evening or weekend events and ability to travel to on and off campus event locations. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: One (1) year of professional program, outreach, or event coordination experience. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of outreach and marketing strategies. Knowledge of clerical and administrative procedures and systems such as filing and record-keeping. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office products. Ability to multitask and prioritize assignments. Additional Job Details Preferences: Experience using Google Workspace, Mailchimp, Canva, and similar design products. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Ability to independently manage competing priorities in a complex and dynamic environment. Strong interpersonal and communication skills Required Application Materials: Cover letter and resume   Best Consideration Date:  August 14, 2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled:  Yes   Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department CMNS-Computer Science Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $38,795 - $41,300 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
