    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Director--Accounts-Payable_JR104455": {
      "title": "Director, Accounts Payable",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organizational Summary Statement The Director of Accounts Payable provides administrative oversight for the University's Accounts Payable function. The position reports to the Assistant Vice President for Procurement and Business Services, and is responsible for establishing the vision, priorities, and operational strategy for accounts payable services across the institution. The Director ensures the timely, accurate, and compliant disbursement of payments while advancing operational excellence, financial stewardship, customer service, and continuous improvement in support of the University's academic, research, and administrative missions. The Director serves as the senior leader for Accounts Payable and oversees the Assistant Directors of Accounts Payable and their teams. The role is responsible for departmental operations, performance management, internal controls, and service delivery across centralized and delegated accounts payable operations. This role ensures that vendors are paid timely, accurately, and in accordance with University of Maryland, USM, and State of Maryland policies and procedures. As a member of the Procurement and Business Services leadership team, the Director serves as an advisor to the Assistant Vice President and collaborates with campus and system partners to improve financial operations, modernize business processes, and support enterprise initiatives. The Director ensures compliance with University policy, State of Maryland regulations, federal requirements, and generally accepted accounting principles. About Accounts Payable at the University of Maryland, College Park The Accounts Payable department supports the University's financial integrity by processing payments to vendors, contractors, employees, students, and other stakeholders. As part of the Division of Finance, the function ensures timely and accurate disbursement of funds in support of academic, research, and administrative operations while maintaining strong internal controls and exceptional service to the campus community. Physical Demands: Work is performed in an office environment and requires the ability to operate standard office equipment and keyboards. Must have the ability to lift and small carry parcels, packages and other items, to walk short distances, and drive a vehicle to deliver and pick up materials. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Ten (10) years of professional accounting or finance experience. Five (5) years of experience supervising or managing professional staff. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of core accounts payable processes and accounting systems. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office and Google Suite products. Ability to multitask and prioritize assignments. Ability to exercise independent judgment and discretion. Ability to develop and administer new policies and procedures. Additional Job Details Preferences: Experience with Workday or comparable ERP system Experience in higher education or large, complex organizations Experience leading process improvement and technology initiatives Demonstrated success leading high performing teams and cross functional collaboration Accounts Payables experience with a large organization Required Application Materials: Resume, Cover Letter, List of References Best Consideration Date: August 7, 2026 Posting Close Date: N/A Open Until Filled: Yes. Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required Yes For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department VPF - Accounts Payable Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range 181,920.00 - 218,304.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Plant-Research-Growth-Facility-Manager_JR104038": {
      "title": "Plant Research Growth Facility Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Position Summary/Purpose of Position: This position is responsible for managing the daily functions of the University of Maryland Plant Research Growth Facility, housed in the Research Greenhouse Complex and Plant Sciences buildings. The Manager shall be responsible for the maintenance of the research plant material grown in the facility. This position is in the category of an Essential Employee. Job duties: • Manage all greenhouse and growth chamber-related operations: Plant care and space management (60%) o Assign and allocate greenhouse bench space, growth chamber space, use of exterior screen houses, cold frame areas, and facility storage areas. o Implement and conduct plant management practices involving water, fertilizer, and pest control. o Set and monitor environmental controls; troubleshoot and replace or repair Priva equipment o Responsible for Worker Protection Standard (WPS) Compliance and Training of all greenhouse users o Monitor and confirm functionality of all environmental controls. o Work with PSLA Facilities Manager to resolve all maintenance needs. o Monitor space usage and assign monthly bench charges. o Manage and enforce proper greenhouse cleanliness and organization of common areas. • Personnel management: Supervise and train greenhouse employees. Plant and prioritize their daily tasks and duties and communicate user needs for specialized plant care. Monitor and measure employee performance and resolve problems as needed. All administrative duties for timesheet approvals for greenhouse personnel. (20%) • Material and supply management: Purchase and maintain inventory of plant care supplies including fertilizer and pesticides. Contact vendors to solicit donations of greenhouse supplies. Maintain pesticide materials and records to meet all state and federal requirements. All administrative duties for purchasing greenhouse supplies and materials. (10%) • Perform other duties as necessary in support of Department goals and objectives, and objectives of Plant Research Growth Facility, to include but not limited to: (10%) o Lead tour groups for both internal and external stakeholders o Guest lecturer for classes held at the Research Greenhouse Complex Preferred: Master of Science in Plant Science or related field; Experience with automated greenhouse controls (Priva, Wadsworth, or similar systems); experience with Integrated Pest Management Methods. Experience in the production and support of plant-based research preferred. Ability to effectively manage priorities and create strong working relations with other campus Departments; Exceptional numerical, organizational, and communication skills; Pest scouting skills and experience. Ability to run the fork lift or obtain required training within 6 months. Licenses: Maryland Pesticide Applicator License required or obtained within a six month period of initial hiring date Schedule: Must be available for irregular schedule; Must be available to work/ on call for weekends; Must be available to work Holidays, catastrophic weather conditions, etc. Physical Demands: Some lifting, working in wet or humid weather conditions, requires hazardous material safety, working environment may have allergens (i.e. dust, grasses, etc.) must wear and work in personal protection clothing. Salary and Benefits: Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. The University of Maryland offers an extensive benefits package. Applications: All candidates must apply online. Please submit an application letter, resume/CV, copy of transcripts and the names and contact information for three professional references. Additional Information: This position may be subject to a Criminal History Record Check and the University of Maryland Background Check. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and clearance of both the Criminal History Record Check and the University of Maryland Background Check, as applicable. The University reserves the right to rescind offers of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Offers are contingent on providing proof of employment eligibility in the United States no more than 3 days after the initial start date. If this proof is not provided within this timeframe, the offer may be rescinded, or employment terminated. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. \n \nExperience: Three (3) years of greenhouse production experience. One (1) year of experience leading or supervising professional staff. \n \nOther: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. Knowledge of greenhouse production.\nSkill in oral and written communication.\nSkill in the use of Microsoft Office products. \nAbility to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws.\nAbility to multitask while demonstrating a commitment to customer service and sensitivity to a culturally and ethnically diverse community. Additional Job Details Preferences: Required Application Materials: Please submit an application letter, resume/CV, copy of transcripts, and the names and contact information for three professional references   Best Consideration Date: August 7 , 2026   Posting Close Date:   Open Until Filled: Yes   Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-Plant Science & Landscape Architecture Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $75,273 - $90,327 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/UHR-HR-Generalist_JR104412": {
      "title": "UHR HR Generalist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information Organization's Summary Statement: University Human Resources Operations is seeking a detail-oriented and service-driven HR Generalist to join our team. This position is a critical front-line resource, providing comprehensive HR customer service and operational support to campus HR Analysts, employees, and other stakeholders. The HR Generalist responds to inquiries across a wide range of human resources functions, including benefits, recruitment, training, HR transactions, and general HR policies and procedures. In this role, you will serve as the primary point of contact for campus users, providing guidance, troubleshooting support, and process navigation related to core HR systems and procedures. This role involves troubleshooting, testing, and partnering with HR and Workday teams to resolve complex issues. Systems include ServiceNow, Workday, State of Maryland Systems, and other campus-based systems. Success in this role requires the ability to manage multiple priorities, navigate and understand complex systems, communicate clearly and empathetically, adapt quickly to changes, and provide accurate and timely support. A strong customer service mindset and the ability to translate complex HR concepts into clear guidance are essential. This role plays a key part in delivering responsive, knowledgeable, and effective HR services to the campus community. Position duties  – T he incumbent of the position will :  Serve  as a first point of contact for campus customers by responding to routine HR inquiries via phone, email, and/or ticketing system, providing timely and courteous customer service. Provide basic HR support across a range of functional areas, including benefits, recruitment, onboarding, training, payroll, and general HR policies and procedures. Perform  standard HR transactions and data entry using core HR systems, ensuring accuracy and compliance with established processes. Provide guidance to campus users on routine HR processes and system navigation, using job aids, documentation, and established procedures. Research and respond to common HR questions using available resources and knowledge base materials; escalate non-routine or complex issues to appropriate HR staff as needed. Support the HR Generalist team during peak service periods by assisting with workload volume and maintaining service levels. Maintain confidentiality of employee information and adhere to university policies, procedures, and data security requirements. This is a C1 Contractual position working up to 40 hours per week, up to 6 months. Physical Demands: Because of its customer service nature, this is an in-office position that adheres to a standard work schedule. The majority of time is spent sitting at a desk at a computer workstation, and moving around the office to assist customers. Limited travel around the campus, and off-campus, may be necessary. Required Application Materials: Resume , Cover Letter   Best Consideration Date: July 31st , 2026   Posting Close Date: NA   Open Until Filled:  Yes   Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Three (3) years of professional human resources experience. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities: Knowledge of human resources policies and procedures, and federal, state, and other applicable human resources related laws, rules, regulations, and ordinances. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office products. Skill in troubleshooting system errors. Ability to multi-task and prioritize assignments. Ability to analyze situations and determine the best recourse for response. Department VPA-University Human Resources Worker Sub-Type Staff Contractual (C1) (Fixed Term) Salary Range $32-34.41 per hour Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
