    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Senior-Executive-Chef_JR104324": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Chef",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Senior Executive Chef provides strategic culinary leadership for Dining Services by overseeing food quality, menu innovation, sustainability initiatives, and culinary operations across multiple dining venues. Serving as the culinary ambassador for the department, this position leads and develops Executive Chefs, culinary managers, and specialized program areas while ensuring exceptional guest experiences, operational excellence, and alignment with organizational goals. The Senior Executive Chef collaborates closely with campus and community partners, including nutrition and sustainability teams, to advance initiatives related to allergen management, nutrition education, sustainable food systems, local sourcing, food security, and environmental stewardship. This position provides direct supervision of the leaders responsible for the Bakery and Green Dining which include the Terp Farm, and the campus food pantry. Physical Demands: This is an essential position and incumbent must report to work when the campus is closed due to weather or other emergency situations. Must be able to work a variable schedule including weekends, nights, evenings, and holidays. Annual leave will not be granted for specific periods including the weeks preceding and right after the start of each semester, Maryland Day, Family Weekend or special events. Must have the manual dexterity to operate equipment with or without accommodation and to lift up to 15 pounds regularly. The University of Maryland is a non-smoking, drug-free, weapon-free campus. Must be able to lift 40 pounds on a regular basis and up to 75 pounds occasionally and stand, walk and work on feet for long periods of time. Must be able to work in extreme weather, humidity and temperature conditions including regularly working between 40 degrees and 90 degrees for extended periods and, from 15 below zero degrees to 40 degrees and from 90 degrees to 110 degrees for short periods of time. Licenses/ Certifications: Must have and maintain Prince George’s County Maryland Certified Food Service Manager Certification and ServSafe Certification within 90 days of hire. Must have driver’s license valid in Maryland with 5 points or less. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: Eight (8) years of progressively responsible experience in culinary operations or food service management. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES:  Knowledge of best practices in management of a high-volume food service operation. Knowledge of staff supervision best practices. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office and Google Workspace products. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Ability to multitask while demonstrating a commitment to customer service. Additional Job Details Preferences: Experience in higher education dining, healthcare, hospitality, contract food service, or other complex multi-unit food service environments. Experience leading sustainability, local sourcing, farm-to-table, food recovery, food security, or environmental stewardship initiatives. Experience partnering with dietitians and nutrition professionals on allergen management and special dietary accommodation programs. Experience managing budgets, forecasting, purchasing, and food cost controls. Experience with employee engagement and leadership development programs. FoodPro knowledge. Required Application Materials: Cover Letter and Resume   Best Consideration Date: August 7, 2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department VPSA-Dining Services Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $110,800 - $132,960 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Coordinator_JR104366": {
      "title": "Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Business Office Coordinator provides comprehensive support across human resources, payroll, procurement, travel & events coordination, facilities, asset management, and web operations within the department. This role ensures efficient onboarding and payroll processing, oversees student employment, manages procurement and facilities operations, and maintains the department’s digital presence. The position collaborates closely with the Business office, faculty, and central administrative units to ensure operational excellence, compliance, and effective communication. Physical Demands: N/A Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: One (1) year of professional human resources, payroll, finance, accounting, procurement, or travel coordination experience. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of human resources policies and procedures, and federal, state, and other applicable human resources related laws, rules, regulations, and ordinances. Skill in oral and written communication. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office and Google Suite products. Ability to multi-task and prioritize assignments. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Additional Job Details Preferences: Familiarity with web design and social media tools preferred Workday knowledge Knowledge of UMD campus services and systems Excellent customer service skills Computer proficiency; competency in MS Suite applications Required Application Materials: Resume Cover Letter List of References   Best Consideration Date: 07/31/2026   Posting Close Date: NA   Open Until Filled: Yes   Additional Information: This position is fully in-person. Telework and remote work are not available. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position Physical Demands: Must be able to lift and move up to 50lbs at a time Ability to travel throughout the department as requested Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required Yes For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department CMNS-Mathematics Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $55,680 - $65,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
