    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/HR---Payroll-Coordinator_JR103649": {
      "title": "HR & Payroll Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Center for Global Sustainability (CGS) at the University of Maryland seeks an HR & Payroll Coordinator to provide operational support for human resources and payroll administration. This position supports the day-to-day execution of HR and payroll processes, including processing HR transactions in Workday, supporting payroll and timekeeping compliance, maintaining employee records, and coordinating onboarding activities. The HR & Payroll Coordinator assists with personnel administration for faculty, staff, students, and contingent employees, ensuring transactions are processed accurately and in compliance with university policies and procedures. This role works closely with CGS leadership, School of Public Policy administration, and central university offices to support efficient HR and payroll operations. The position reports to the Manager of Human Resources and plays a key role in maintaining accurate employment records, supporting payroll reporting and compliance, and assisting with the coordination of HR administrative processes across the Center. Essential Duties & Responsibilities: Human Resources Transactions -Initiate and process HR transactions in Workday including hires, job changes, end job actions, and additional pay entries. -Assist with preparation and routing of offer letters, PTK faculty contracts, student appointment documentation, and other employment records. -Maintain personnel documentation and ensure employee records are complete and properly maintained. -Track appointment end dates, contract renewals, and funding changes to ensure timely personnel actions. -Coordinate onboarding processes for new employees including employment documentation and administrative setup. -Assist with tracking and documentation for Form I-9 employment eligibility verification to support compliance requirements. -Route HR forms and supporting documentation for review and approval. Payroll Processing & Timekeeping -Monitor and review employee time entry to ensure accuracy and compliance with university payroll policies. -Track payroll deadlines and ensure required actions are completed in a timely manner. -Process payroll adjustments and corrections in coordination with the appropriate campus payroll offices. -Support entry and monitoring of additional pay transactions. -Assist with payroll reconciliation activities and payroll reporting. -Monitor student employment appointments to ensure compliance with university FTE limits. -Coordinate with the School of Public Policy Business Office and Central Payroll regarding payroll matters and issue resolution. Compliance & Reporting Support -Track HR compliance requirements related to employment documentation and payroll administration. -Maintain HR and payroll tracking reports and internal documentation. -Run and review Workday reports to support HR operations and payroll monitoring. -Assist with preparation of documentation for audits or internal reviews. Other Duties -Provide administrative and operational support for HR functions within CGS. -Assist with onboarding logistics and coordination for new employees. -Perform other duties as assigned in support of HR and payroll operations. Physical Demands: General office duties and tasks, may need to occasionally lift boxes with papers and other documents, up to 20lbs. This is primarily sedentary work. Repetitive typing motions involved. Work takes place in both an office environment and in on-campus buildings; will require ability to travel throughout campus. While position is not physically demanding, incumbent must be able to perform well under strict deadlines. Licenses/ Certifications: Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience: One (1) year of professional human resources or payroll experience. Other: Additional work experience as defined above may be substituted on a year for year basis for up to four (4) years of the required education. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of human resources policies and procedures, and federal, state, and other applicable human resources related laws, rules, regulations, and ordinances. Knowledge of payroll functions. Skill in the use of Microsoft Office products. Ability to multi-task and prioritize assignments. Ability to analyze situations and determine the best recourse for response. Additional Job Details Preferences: Additional Information: UMD will not sponsor the successful candidate for work authorization in the United States now or in the future. Required Application Materials: - Cover Letter - Resume - References   Best Consideration Date:  - April 18, 2026 Posting Close Date:   Open Until Filled:  Yes Job Risks Not Applicable to This Position Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department PLCY - Center for Global Sustainability Worker Sub-Type Staff Regular Salary Range $55,800.00 - $65,760.00 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Exempt benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
